{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions","id":1385487,"title":"Confession time - I just can't get into the Traditions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-03T17:44:04-07:00","id":1385487,"title":"Confession time - I just can't get into the Traditions","content":"I can't get into the Traditions. I'm sorry, I just can't. I can play Technocracy games [and think they're magnificently evil] but the Traditions just don't make sense to me.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy are my favorite types of villains. I described Bester from Babylon Five as the best example when writing a villain. &quot;Bester [as played by Walter Koenig] is a brutal, ruthless, sadistic, and evil bastard. However, Bester can explain to you in three sentences or less what his motivation is in a way that is consistent and understandable even if it's not necessarily sympathetic.&quot; The Technocracy is a totalitarian conspiracy of magical fasists and authoritarians who suppress the Truth of the world and carry out daily atrocities. However, they are people who are justified by their belief society will fall apart if people knew and are nominally against equally bad factions. It's not so much that there's a bunch of rotten eggs and good people, it's that most of the members are combinations of both. Even the bad ones genuinely believe they're leading into a Utopia--it's just they don't care what means are needed to do it. Oh and why not wet your beak while doing it. They are 100% confidant that they are succeeding too--even when they're not.<br /> <br /> The problem with the Traditions is the fact that they are based on Grant Morrison's Invisibles to an extent and are meant to be the plucky resistance to the Technocracy's Illuminati. They're Neo and his ragtag band of Virtual Adepts freeing humanity from its mind-prison. The problem is that's not really a very good thing for the World of Darkness as, unlike the Anarchs, this doesn't really have much of a shades of gray type feel.Some fans overcompensate by saying, &quot;The Traditions are actually a bunch of people fighting against toilets, lights, and vaccines! They're a bunch of Luddite terrorists!&quot;<br /> <br /> This is completely irreconcilable with the way they're presented. They are a collection of Buddhists, Mad Scientists, Christians, Thuggee, and Witches who are all united by their desire to help mankind. If they can overcome that, they're not going to sweat indoor plumbing. You could play up the tensions between the Traditions but it can't reach the level of being actual enemies or even &quot;enemies after we beat the Union&quot; because that's not their thing. They're not nine different organizations allied against the Union, they're one organization with a broad tent.<br /> <br /> As such, they feel too optimistic for the setting but if you change them to a bunch of reactionary bigots, the organization no longer makes sense. Oddly, I think the game woulds make more sense if you just ditched the Traditions entirely and instead just had the players be Orphans and Hollow Ones on the run from the Union's pogrom. They've won and now they're exterminating anyone who won't toe the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T17:59:53-07:00","id":1385492,"title":"","content":"You may want to look into the Disparates. They're another faction that's gathering to oppose the Technocracy; and unlike the Traditions, they <i>are</i> a bunch of separate groups held together only by their opposition to the Union.<br /> <br /> (Incidentally, they include the Hollow Ones; and Orphans are listed under their \u201cumbrella\u201d \u2014 though that's more a matter of the Disparates being something of an \u201c\u2026and the rest\u201d faction.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-03-2020, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T18:08:54-07:00","id":1385495,"title":"","content":"I mean fair enough, I don't entirely agree but I see your point.<br /> <br /> Before I get into a longer response, was this post more of an essay thread or an invitation for people to attempt changing your mind? Not trying to be a smart ass or anything, legit just trying to read the room before I dip in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T18:15:16-07:00","id":1385497,"title":"","content":"I would point out that while the Traditions do have flaws, \u201cdoesn't like indoor plumbing\u201d isn't one of them. <i>Nobody</i> in Mage is insane enough not to like the benefits of technology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T18:29:18-07:00","id":1385499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1385495#post1385495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean fair enough, I don't entirely agree but I see your point.<br /> <br /> Before I get into a longer response, was this post more of an essay thread or an invitation for people to attempt changing your mind? Not trying to be a smart ass or anything, legit just trying to read the room before I dip in.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm open to suggestions. I may be completely wrong. I always welcome critique of my ideas. You don't get very far in writing if you can't take a different opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T19:02:03-07:00","id":1385506,"title":"","content":"I think you've hit on the crux of the issue with your comparison. Mage isn't Vampire, it's not built on a degenerative framework. Mage: the <b>Ascension </b>is about striving for improvement, surpassing your limits and overcoming your own weaknesses. Outside of Golconda stories this is generally not how Vampire functions, occasionally you'll see a point or two when things start sliding far. Mage on the other had starts low and works upward. So yes if the Traditions succeed the world will be better, that's the point of the game. It's not about fighting a battle with your own moral degeneration but about pushing past your preconceptions to envision a brighter world.<br /> <br /> As for the Traditions describing their motivations, they're all looking to bring magic and wonder back into the world. It's why they can have two fundamentally technological organizations under the same umbrella. The Technocracy is an organization that removes the spontaneity from existence. The idea of a single firebrand radically changing the landscape with an idea is fundamentally anathema to their goals. They want everything to be slow, controlled, boring, and eventually static. A world of grey dull things where independent thought is crushed under the weight of social conditioning. Meanwhile the Etherites and Adepts believe that individuality is key to innovation and things can, and should, advance in leaps and bounds.<br /> <br /> Overall the view you posit on the World of Darkness is one that's too dark. Instead of a world worse off then our own you want one that's unremittingly dark where all hope is crushed and the characters are practically insignificant points against a victorious monster. Mage is about that one person being able to awaken themselves to a potential to fix that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T19:24:31-07:00","id":1385514,"title":"","content":"Very well done, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2008\" data-vbnamecard=\"2008\">Cynic01</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T19:35:03-07:00","id":1385517,"title":"","content":"That's definitely been the message of earlier editions, yes. But how is it a game about one mage being able to change everything if you basically need the backing of the Traditions if you want to have any hope of changing anything? Frankly, a game where the protagonists are Orphans who are capable of upsetting the Technocracy speaks much more to the theme of \u201cone man can make a difference\u201d than a game where two organizations (the Traditions and the Technocracy) are fighting an Ascension War. <br /> <br /> What <i>I'm</i> looking for from this thread is an exploration of just what the Traditions' failings are, keeping in mind that they're the Traditions and not the Disparates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T19:50:34-07:00","id":1385520,"title":"","content":"Alrighty so!<br /> <br /> I definitely agree that the Technocratic Union and the spectrum it's been able to achieve over its growth these editions is really cool and makes them fantastic both as hard core villains, sympathetic villains, anti-heroes, and even the occasional genuine hero in the mix.<br /> <br /> I think that when looking at the Council of Traditions, it's useful to look at them as being surprisingly similar to the Union but of a radically different paradigm. This is also how I can go about differentiating them from the Disparates and Orphans. <br /> <br /> Let me explain. The Council of Traditions, if this were a millennium ago, could not exist because of the radical differences between its members. Their are deep divisive lines between and within every tradition. At many times the entire construct of 'tradition' fails to truly accommodate the Willworkers within. Yet, there is a reason why the Traditions are distinct from the Disparate Council despite their similarities. The recent creation of the latter aside, the Disparate Council is ultimately defined as something of a loose confederation of crafts trying to survive and being willing to help each other to do so. This is definitely similar to the Council, but the main difference is scope and scale. The Council of Traditions hasn't just banded together for mutual survival: they want to win.<br /> <br /> The Council of Traditions is made up of nine traditions, most of whom are ancient and powerful in their own rights. Their radical departure from the Union is their refusal to limit the scope of reality. Each one has a distinct paradigm and distinct goals but they are united by their desire to undermine and replace the Technocratic paradigm that currently dominates much of the world.<br /> <br /> The Traditions are the scions of the pre-Union world. A world that saw reality Balkanized between Willworkers and vicious battles for dominance between them and the self-proclaimed rite and privelage to steward humanity and its development. Many will-workers see guiding humanity as a duty and obligation and the Technocratic Union and Council of Traditions are identical in their zeal to uphold this duty. Few on either side stopped to ask whether humanity would actually want either side's help.<br /> <br /> If humanity actually wanted a world defined by concrete and immovable laws, where society was led by an enlightened few and the ultimate goal was a utopia of progression, safety, and security. If humanity wanted a world defined by magic and mysticism where anyone had the potential to wield the cosmic forces of the universe and bend them to their will, leading nations like-unto god-kings. Perhaps there are many who would support either vision, yet there would also be many horrified by either vision.<br /> <br /> The Council of Traditions and Technocratic Union both have many sympathetic ideals and pursuits and traits, but they are also both defined by an unwavering sense of Hubris. They both feel it is their right and duty to lead humanity to the One True Utopia they invision.<br /> <br /> Prior to the rise of the Order of Reason, most traditions (as they were then) couldn't stand each other and many will-workers actively battled over reality. What has bound them tougher is little more then a vague ideal as a common purpose and the understood common threat that the Technocracy represents. They need each other if they want to win the Ascension War. Once the Union's threat is dissolved, its back to each other's throats in the battle to ensure that reality takes The Right Path.<br /> <br /> Yet, this broad similarly isn't alone what interests me about the Council, or its relatively more accessible paradigm. It's the sheer amount of tensions between and within the traditions.<br /> <br /> Each tradition has a piece of beautiful truth and revelatory secrets. They also each are marred by terrible flaws. The Hermetics defined reality but are the heights of Hubris and domineering elitism. The Choristers are exemplary at creating social cohesion while simultaneously being buffeted by schism brought about by faith near-constantly. The Society of Ether offers a miraculous world of science while also having incredibly bizarre limits placed by their own zealously defended prejudices.<br /> <br /> The traditions each have long histories yet aside from perhaps the Order of Hermes, only this era could make them. Many traditions are loose structures connecting a vast spectrum of ideals and paradigms that loosely interweave. This balkanizes them all from within while they simultaneously bristle from proximity to the other traditions. Bloodshed, prejudice, atrocity, disdain, and loathing are liberally scattered across their histories and anything could set these proud will-workers against each other.<br /> <br /> Yet... they are still bound by a common virtue. The idea that humanity should have the freedom to embrace visions of reality beyond the static ideal that the Technocratic Union provides. Yes that reality may be dangerous and it may be unpredictable... but it was within the reach of anyone with the capacity to recognize it was there. To reach out and make the world their own. To defy the definitions of what could and couldn't be. To do utterly and freely as they Will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T20:10:37-07:00","id":1385524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions#post1385487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with the Traditions is the fact that they are based on Grant Morrison's Invisibles to an extent and are meant to be the plucky resistance to the Technocracy's Illuminati.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the idea that the Traditions are based on a comic that came out after Mage was first published would be a very impressively Mage thing to pull off...<br /> <br /> Though to add to Cynic01's point about being overly biased by framing things via VtM, trying too hard to frame the Traditions in other pop culture is also going to lead to unsatisfactory results. Mage is by no means an attempt to keep itself separate from cultural influences from sources like The Invisibles or the Matrix (both have been cited by the books over the years as good inspirational material), but that doesn't make the Traditions whatever other cultural expression they resemble.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The problem is that's not really a very good thing for the World of Darkness as, unlike the Anarchs, this doesn't really have much of a shades of gray type feel. </div> </div> </div>I think the problem (discounting the people that are very wrong about the Traditions and technology; as I love to point out the Chakravanti created vaccines long before modern medicine figured it out) is that the shades of grey aren't really in the Council of Nine Traditions as an organization.<br /> <br /> This is one of the ways the VtM vs. MtA comparison is very flawed. The Camarilla vs. the Sabbat vs. the Anarchs in whatever combination doesn't really need to get into the nitty-gritty of each internal faction to understand the shades of grey of the game.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy, as befits it's origin as &quot;The Monolith&quot; of a single organizational enemy, is easy to view as a whole no matter how detailed you can get about it's internal structure and factions.<br /> <br /> The Traditions started as an alliance of convenience to fight the Order of Reason that's lasted long enough that most Tradition members have only known that alliance and manufactured new reasons to perpetuate its existence. But you can't look at the shades of grey by looking at the whole all that well. To get into my own comparison, trying to get into the issues of the NATO alliance continuing past the Cold War is fairly hard without actually examining at least some of the individual member nations; and how that reflects on the whole when you realize what that means the organization will tolerate from its members.<br /> <br /> If you don't get into the shades of grey of each Tradition, which are present in spades when you look into them, missing the shades of grey in the Traditions as a whole is inevitable.<br /> <br /> Without getting into a breakdown of each Tradition, a simple summary is fairly direct: the Traditions are fighting for a meritocratic society where they have inherently more merit by valuing magical power as the ultimate merit to society. If the Code of Ananda following Cultists won the right to define that society, things would be pretty good for humanity really. If the Order of Hermes dictated things, quintessence would be the basis of all economic systems and those that can control/manipulate it become the new billionaire class.. but they can fireball anyone that complains about it. If the Golden Chalice had it's way... well the setting would flip to the Technocracy being the good guys no matter how fascistic.<br /> <br /> And when you consider that the people that want to create a utopia where magic users ensure a post-scarcity society and humanity can reach it's ultimately potential are working with people that believe in extrajudicial murder as a tenet of faith to enact on the whims of fate... well it's not really a situation lacking in the moral gray of compromise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You could play up the tensions between the Traditions but it can't reach the level of being actual enemies or even &quot;enemies after we beat the Union&quot; because that's not their thing. They're not nine different organizations allied against the Union, they're one organization with a broad tent. </div> </div> </div>This is exceedingly at odds with how the Traditions have always been written.<br /> <br /> The Traditions have been having internal violent conflicts for as long as they've existed, and even after centuries of alliance, they remain distinct organizations (and who the nine are has changed a bunch of times) that would struggle to remain unified if the Union, and Nephandi, and the Marauders, were ever defeated in full.<br /> <br /> &quot;We're all unified beyond the Ascension War!&quot; isn't the truth, it's Tradition spin on a hope that's never been tested, and with lots of reasons to doubt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As such, they feel too optimistic for the setting but if you change them to a bunch of reactionary bigots, the organization no longer makes sense. </div> </div> </div>For the talk of &quot;gray&quot; in the setting... this is one hell of an excluded middle.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T21:42:34-07:00","id":1385534,"title":"","content":"Or to put it a different way...Mage's brand of personal horror is VERY different from Vampire's.<br /> <br /> Vampire it's a lot more passive and inherent: it's about the Curse of Caine that resides in all of the Kindred, and how their imposed condition fundamentally changes the way they live their life, with all the factions surrounding it informing how each vampire chooses to deal with the Curse. Conflict between Kindred comes from how they should all deal with it, as well as who deserves the right to blood the most.<br /> <br /> Mage it involves active engagement: hubris. Mages, due to being Awakened/Enlightened to the nature of reality and how to manipulate it, believe they have a duty shape the world into a better place in their eyes. Hubris comes from them not considering what others want reality to be, or thinking they can dismiss any arguments to the contrary because they believe they know better. The whole crux of the Ascension War is because all of the factions have different ideas of how reality should be shaped, and can't agree. All while be willfully ignorant of the ordinary people who would be affected the most as collateral.<br /> <br /> While the method of execution on expressing the personal horror is similar, the actual core of the horror conflict is not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 05-04-2020, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T22:33:08-07:00","id":1385541,"title":"","content":"My personal take has always been that the Traditions are mainly about individuality in a world that generally tends to skew against that, but are often hampered by the hubris which seems to be an inate part of being Awakened. The Ascension War isn't everyone's cup of tea. However, I think there is a lot of fun to be had with the various Crafts as a traditional urban fantasy set up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T12:59:21-07:00","id":1385640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1385524#post1385524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is exceedingly at odds with how the Traditions have always been written.<br /> <br /> The Traditions have been having internal violent conflicts for as long as they've existed, and even after centuries of alliance, they remain distinct organizations (and who the nine are has changed a bunch of times) that would struggle to remain unified if the Union, and Nephandi, and the Marauders, were ever defeated in full.<br /> <br /> &quot;We're all unified beyond the Ascension War!&quot; isn't the truth, it's Tradition spin on a hope that's never been tested, and with lots of reasons to doubt.</div> </div> </div> </div>To add to this. Propaganda it's a word often said in relation with the Technocracy, but the Traditions have a lot of propaganda of their own. Them being harmless hippies that want to bring love and compromise to the world being the foremost of that.<br /> <br /> I mean, sure a world of wonder and compromise it's the general idea...but then again, the idea of the Technocracy as dictated by the White Tower it's one of a humanity uplifted by technology, not one under the wise and benevolent heels of hidden masters.<br /> <br /> Most of the big tragic events on the Mage Lore was at least partially caused by Traditional internal strife. From Voormass &quot;actions&quot; being purposely hidden by the Euthanatos (because they had it totally under control, and didn't want to be judged by <s>the Akashicks</s> the other Traditions) to the Hermetics acting like they own the place (and indirectly causing the fall of Horizon by pissing off the Hollow Ones too much). Or the Porthos vs. Mustai conflict that brought down Doissetep. That Verbena aren't openly figthing the Choristers it's trully a miracle, that shows how bad the Technocracy hit them, but I hope you weren't playing a Janissary in 2e, because in 3e you are being chased by the Euthanatos over a perceived treachery that most likely you weren't even part of (well, not consciously at least).<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Under the general umbrella of &quot;Freedom&quot; and &quot;Wonder&quot; that the Traditions represent there's a lot of space for bigotry, darkness, evil and internal fight.<br /> <br /> Like how you're forbbiden to be an infernalist...except that &quot;demon&quot; it's a very subjective concept (aka: &quot;your demon it's my horned fertility god&quot;), so you can totally be an infernalist as long as you don't use that word. Or maybe you don't perceive yourself as an infernalist, more as an anty-sistem magician, but sure the Guardian Orders of the Chorus next door, that dedicate their lives to hunt demons, are of a different opinion...the Law of an off-world <s>bag of cats</s> Council, and fear of the Hit-Marks are the only thing that stands between their holly swords an your new age grove.<br /> <br /> There's stories to tell right there that either don't involve figthing the Technocracy at all, or have it as an outside force that exists as a shadow of menace were things to escalate too far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-04-2020, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T13:52:46-07:00","id":1385649,"title":"","content":"To add to the addition to my post with an anecdote:<br /> <br /> One of my PCs almost killed another PC over the infernalism thing. My PC was very much in the &quot;infernalism = Nephandi = kill ASAP&quot; mindset, and meeting the other PC resulted in a understandably bad in-game personality conflict. This was then followed by a very poorly worded attempt to say that LaVeyan Satanism wasn't wrong (mostly poorly worded by not getting to the point of &quot;I don't actually believe in worshiping evil deities&quot;), and well... fortunately other characters stepped in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T14:20:11-07:00","id":1385653,"title":"","content":"I would point out that Mage: The Ascension\u2019s Traditions were, in fact, written before Grant Morrisons\u2019 The Invisibles - and the similarities between the two are merely coincidental. I guess that mysticism and magic was a big thing in the 1990s. <br /> <br /> I used to play Mage a lot - it was my major game playing through University years (in the 1990s) and it was my first WoD game (before I played Vampire). Over the years, I felt that the Traditions could have been done better if the were more a category of the general paradigm of players, rather than group affiliations. So instead of bespoke organizations around each Tradition, they would simply refer to the \u2019tradition\u2019 of the mage being Hermetic, Wiccan, Zen, Theistic, Shamanic, and so on. I\u2019d have then had some broad church, secret society group affiliations which the characters could join up to - possibly including The Order of Hermes from Ars Magica with several houses that drew upon an eclectic range of mages from different paradigms. I could have seen the Etherites and Virtual Adepts standing apart from the Traditions too. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T17:27:08-07:00","id":1385690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions#post1385487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is completely irreconcilable with the way they're presented.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny, I've never had an issue with thinking of them as terrorists. The Technocrcy are fascists autocrats trying to bring about a Shiny Black Mirror World. The Traditions are terrorists who do not care about the common people, or those caught in the cross fire. They care about their bruised egos, and to a one would usher in a world just as vile, if they could. Members of the traditions make better horror movie monsters and villains than they do heroes.<br /> <br /> This is the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> There are no heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":".  Porthos made me do it. 05-04-2020, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T14:42:52-07:00","id":1386180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1385690#post1385690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Funny, I've never had an issue with thinking of them as terrorists. The Technocrcy are fascists autocrats trying to bring about a Shiny Black Mirror World. The Traditions are terrorists who do not care about the common people, or those caught in the cross fire. They care about their bruised egos, and to a one would usher in a world just as vile, if they could. Members of the traditions make better horror movie monsters and villains than they do heroes.<br /> <br /> This is the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> There are no heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sounds more like a headcannon than what any books ever said about the Traditions. Literally every book is about the creation of a better world, about them caring about sleepers and avoiding casualties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T15:29:15-07:00","id":1386185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386180#post1386180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds more like a headcannon than what any books ever said about the Traditions. Literally every book is about the creation of a better world, about them caring about sleepers and avoiding casualties.</div> </div> </div> </div>Friend: But Euthanatos KILL people.<br /> <br /> Me: Bad people!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T15:48:39-07:00","id":1386196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386185#post1386185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Friend: But Euthanatos KILL people.<br /> <br /> Me: Bad people!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which is a literal fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T17:48:14-07:00","id":1386218,"title":"","content":"Well, literal bias. How the Euthanatos select their targets is based in a specific belief system where their definition of bad doesn't mesh with any universal definition of bad. And they don't just kill bad people; they also kill good people for the bad impacts they will have despite their good intentions. The Euthanatos don't have access to the universal naughty and nice list. They're enforcing their morality system on other people violently.<br /> <br /> That said, viewing the Traditions as terrorists or utopians is just looking at the extremes. Most Tradition members are somewhere between the two. Some are attempting to be both extremes at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T20:27:31-07:00","id":1386235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386180#post1386180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds more like a headcannon than what any books ever said about the Traditions. Literally every book is about the creation of a better world, about them caring about sleepers and avoiding casualties.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the books are told from their perspectives, and center on them and their needs and egos. Consider how they appear to the Technocracy, and even to the Disparates. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386185#post1386185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Friend: But Euthanatos KILL people.<br /> <br /> Me: Bad people!</div> </div> </div> </div>In the World of Darkness, &quot;bad people&quot; is almost everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T21:01:27-07:00","id":1386239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386235#post1386235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the books are told from their perspectives, and center on them and their needs and egos. Consider how they appear to the Technocracy, and even to the Disparates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, which doesn't mean it's not true.<br /> <br /> Mind you, a lot of people took the Revised Covention Books as objectively true. The Iteration X book being the worst.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T21:06:16-07:00","id":1386240,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1208_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1208\" data-vbnamecard=\"1208\">Grumpy RPG Reviews</a> you guys make some really good points. Thanks.<br /> <br /> Porthios the Archmage or Porthos the Musketeer? \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T21:50:42-07:00","id":1386250,"title":"","content":"I've never seen the Traditions as people &quot;united to help mankind&quot;. I see them as individuals with private goals who have formed an alliance of convenience in order to stand against a common enemy. That alliance of convenience is a description of both the Council of Nine and each individual Tradition as well.<br /> <br /> And the definition of that alliance can change at any time. At least two Traditions were once members of the Technocracy, and their involvement is only because they became political dissidents within the Union.<br /> <br /> The Traditions certainly have a code of ethics, but I think it's just as effective as other professional code of ethics in Law, Medicine, or any other group. The code allows, justifies, and even requires certain actions that could be considered wrong by other people (use your legal skills so that murderers and rapists escape justice because everyone deserves a legal defense, or use your medical skills to save the lives of murderers and rapists). And the code is also easily ignored so that criminal practitioners use their skills for self-serving purposes and exploit people who come to them for help. Not to mention general sleazy people who may not commit any violations per the ethics code, but still seem pretty sleazy without it.<br /> <br /> Professional codes of ethics tend to be things designed to create pride within the organization that they have standards, and to serve as Marketing/PR to the outside world.<br /> <br /> Power tends to corrupt, and Magick gives people a lot of power.<br /> <br /> So I've never seen them as an organization of White Hats although certain individuals might be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T21:51:26-07:00","id":1386251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386235#post1386235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because the books are told from their perspectives, and center on them and their needs and egos. Consider how they appear to the Technocracy, and even to the Disparates. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In the World of Darkness, &quot;bad people&quot; is almost everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would add that they've got the bulk of the first three editions written from their perspective, which tends to reinforce the impression that they're <i>the</i> good guys. The only exceptions were the Book of Crafts and the Guide to the Technocracy \u2014 and even the Book of Crafts was essentially written from the perspective of the Traditions. As far as the readers are concerned, the Traditions got a solid decade of good press, followed by another decade where nothing derogatory was said about them (though admittedly that's because nothing <i>at all</i> was being said).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-07-2020, 02:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T22:00:05-07:00","id":1386252,"title":"","content":"My inclination is the Euthanatos idea of the &quot;Good Death&quot; is going to apply to:<br /> <br /> * The hopelessly evil<br /> * People whose quality of life is incredibly deteriorated (They're believers in &quot;Mercy Killings&quot;)<br /> * People who killing would improve the world somehow due to Entropy showing chance","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T22:39:06-07:00","id":1386265,"title":"","content":"Akin to what Black Fox just said, a large part of the morality question for Mage is emphasized by the thematic focus of 'Hubris'. Mages by definition are proud, driven, even arrogant. They are classic heroes and villains. Embodiments of Hubris.<br /> <br /> They alter circumstances and reality itself through the sheer force of willpower and wrestling the nature of it into the shape that they see fit. Damn those who disagree, will-workers are self-righteous. Some are truly righteous as well but they must all be unswervingly dedicated to their principles to do what they do.<br /> <br /> By their very nature, this means that many of them defy the restraints of conventional morality. What is the law of Essex County to someone who can bend the so-called laws of physics? Who cares if a few people's death pave the roads to utopia?<br /> <br /> Everything in the world becomes easier to justify when you are absolutely certain of your rightness. Then you take these people and find those with loosely similar opinions regarding reality and give them a loose title to unite them all into nine collectives.<br /> <br /> Then you take these nine collectives and gather them into one political body. Each head of the leviathan intent on reigning supreme and each writhing in a different direction with only the uncaring principles of Metareality and the dubiously moral 'Hero' to hold the sword and shield against it. Chaos bound together only by necessity and conceit.<br /> <br /> This is the Council of Traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T23:44:58-07:00","id":1386282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386252#post1386252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My inclination is the Euthanatos idea of the &quot;Good Death&quot; is going to apply to:<br /> <br /> * The hopelessly evil<br /> * People whose quality of life is incredibly deteriorated (They're believers in &quot;Mercy Killings&quot;)<br /> * People who killing would improve the world somehow due to Entropy showing chance</div> </div> </div> </div>And people that are reincarnations of souls that the Euthanatos don't consider having been sufficiently cleansed of those three things the last time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T23:48:33-07:00","id":1386285,"title":"","content":"With all due respect, I tend to view the \u201cheld together only by necessity and conceit\u201d is more of a Disparate Alliance thing than a Traditions thing. Yes, the Traditions <i>do</i> fight among themselves; but they've got their <i>own</i> version of a \u201cshared truth\u201d that binds them together, and actually facilitates bridge building among them: \u201cWe Are All Gods in Disguise\u201d. When the first Council of Traditions established the shared lingo that allowed mages of nine wildly different traditions to get on the same page when discussing Magick, it established a common ground that let those mages work together with an ease that they had never been able to manage before. One of their strengths is that they're inherently \u201cecumenical\u201d, with their shared belief that they're all practicing the same Art; they're just going about it in different ways. <br /> <br /> They don't always live up to that ideal; but they try to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T23:52:12-07:00","id":1386289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386285#post1386285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With all due respect, I tend to view the \u201cheld together only by necessity and conceit\u201d is more of a Disparate Alliance thing than a Traditions thing. Yes, the Traditions <i>do</i> fight among themselves; but they've got their <i>own</i> version of a \u201cshared truth\u201d that binds them together, and actually facilitates bridge building among them: \u201cWe Are All Gods in Disguise\u201d. When the first Council of Traditions established the shared lingo that allowed mages of nine wildly different traditions to get on the same page when discussing Magick, it established a common ground that let those mages work together with an ease that they had never been able to manage before. One of their strengths is that they're inherently \u201cecumenical\u201d, with their shared belief that they're all practicing the same Art; they're just going about it in different ways.<br /> <br /> They don't always live up to that ideal; but they try to.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the big things that may be influencing my view is the fact that I've never bought into Mage Revised's views that mages don't know that it's all will-working. Dreamspeakers, Hermetics, Technocrats, and so on may all have different tools/foci but they all know how the sausage is made. It's a fight about what tools Sleepers should be presented to use, not a fight over what the nature of awakening is.<br /> <br /> Arguably, it makes the Ascension War an even more psychotic waste of lives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T23:54:29-07:00","id":1386290,"title":"","content":"My take on it is that the <i>Traditions</i> have always believed that it's all Willworking; but that that's <i>their thing</i>, the thing that distinguishes them from both the Technocracy (who at least in TR very clearly do <i>not</i> believe that Awakened Magick and Enlightened Science are the same thing; TR says as much in no uncertain terms) and the Crafts (who, in my view at least, mostly tend not to <i>care</i>, one way or the other). <br /> <br /> Where I firmly agree with you is that the Awakening or Enlightenment is fundamentally a realization that you have an innate quality that gives you the power to change the world, literally. And yes, MRev got it wrong when it said otherwise. But that realization does <i>not</i> innately come with the understanding that everyone else who can shape reality is doing the same thing you are. If that was something that every mage instinctively knows, then it would have been a ubiquitous truth since days long past, before the dawn of history; it would not have been something that the Council of Nine discovered in the 1400s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-07-2020, 03:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T23:56:46-07:00","id":1386292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386290#post1386290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That wasn't a MRev thing; that's something that's been part of the game since the first edition was initially published.</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify, I'm saying that in Revised, they acted like mages DIDN'T know it was all will-working.<br /> <br /> Which was established by things like the Son of Ether scroll, Order of Hermes Paradigm, and all the Tradition books.<br /> <br /> Awakening is when you know reality is by will and really-really believe it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T00:30:59-07:00","id":1386300,"title":"","content":"You'll note that the post that you quoted has been completely rewritten, because I posted it too fast, and based my response on a literal misreading of what you said. I refer you to the rewritten version. <br /> <br /> In particular, I agree that all of the <i>Traditions</i> agree that the inherent power to change the world is Willworking. That agreement is what the Traditions were founded on. That's one reason you'll find \u201cit's all Willworking\u201d in every Tradition Book. <br /> <br /> But outside of the Traditions is a different matter. Sure, there's still a universally shared experience by everyone who Awakens that they have an innate power to change reality. But the interpretation of the <i>nature of</i> that power, outside of the Traditions, is a lot more varied (except in the Union, where it's not surprisingly fairly regimented \u2014 but in a way that's quite different from the Traditions' Willworking notion).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-07-2020, 03:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T01:32:24-07:00","id":1386317,"title":"","content":"In terms of the Technocracy's view of it, let me point out three items: <br /> <br /> The Technocrat term for \u201cAvatar\u201d is \u201cGenius\u201d. <br /> <br /> The Technocrat term for \u201cArete\u201d is \u201cEnlightenment\u201d. <br /> <br /> In the Revised VE Convention Book, the fundamental nature of Tychoidian Cosmology and the Enlightened Anthropic Principle refers to humans as beings who create reality through the processing of information. <br /> <br /> Taken together, the Technocratic conception of \u201cthe power to change reality\u201d is rooted in <i>comprehension and imagination</i> rather than <i>will</i>. <br /> <br /> As for the Disparates, well, it depends on the Disparate. The Batini, Children of Knowledge, and Hollow Ones have all been closely associated with the Traditions and tend to share the Willworking mindset that the Traditions embrace. Heck, the Batini helped <i>invent it</i>. Other factions tend to have explanations in keeping with their Focus: the Sisters of Hypollyta might interpret the power to change reality as something that's rooted in Spontaneity, while the Bata'a might see it as something that derives from a Sensitivity to the Umbra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T05:12:04-07:00","id":1386361,"title":"","content":"Uh....the vast majority of Mages even among the Traditions simply don't realise that its 'will-working' or at least don't agree on what that fundamentally means, the overwhelming bulk of Mages will continue using their Focuses forever and will fundamentally believe in the reality defined by their paradigm til the day they die.<br /> <br /> What needs to be understood is that PCs are not part of that majority and are some of the rare few who possess the ability to grow beyond that if they so choose. Based on the last 20 odd years of play very few even of that number choose to abandon their paradigm and Focus fully.<br /> <br /> Hell, the vast majority of the Masters of the Order of Hermes still use their Focuses even to this day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T07:53:00-07:00","id":1386400,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Try to tell the average Verbena that they're just doing &quot;Willworking&quot;, and that their Old Gods aren't real...<br /> <br /> Of the Traditions, the Akashics might be the closest that consider what they do &quot;Willworking&quot;, Mind over Matter, etc.<br /> Mayhaps followed by the Ecstatics, given that they are all about &quot;Change your perceptions and you can change the world&quot;.<br /> <br /> A VE will just stare at you if you tell him they don't need their fancy computer to do some serious hacking because &quot;It's just your will, bro&quot;, and an Etherite will raise eyebrows if you tell them all their fancy fringe science theories just boil down to &quot;It's just your will doing it!&quot; (Although certain things Etherites do certainly would fall under strange theories of Psionics..but only part of it).<br /> Dreamspeakers will eye you and then maybe say that you need one helluva will to survive harder bargains with Spirits, but the rest is just proper ritual and tradition to address those beings.<br /> <br /> Even dropping instruments does not necessarily equal a Mage starting to believe that they are just working their capital W Will in a literal sense.<br /> A Verbena I've been RPing is a pretty devout fanatic to an old God. Manifest Avatar kind of helps with that. If she starts dropping instruments, it's not because she realizes &quot;I can work my will!&quot;. The opposite, she'll realize the deity is trusting the priestess more and more with potent gifts, while demanding less ritual and etiquette to be granted those blessings.<br /> <br /> Likewise (And I forgot who mentioned it), somebody in another thread mentioned how dropping instruments can also simply mean, in the mind of the mage's paradigm, that they are letting go of training wheels - an Akashic not needing to perform a certain series of Katas anymore in order to attune their Mind for certain things; But this, too, is less a matter of &quot;I am doing Willworking!&quot; and more a matter of simply &quot;My Mind is trained enough to reach the state of &lt;fancy term here&gt; easily now&quot;. It's still well within their first, defined Paradigm.<br /> <br /> The Traditions, as a coherent group, saying &quot;We're just doing willworking guys!&quot; does not mesh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T08:18:08-07:00","id":1386408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386400#post1386400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Traditions, as a coherent group, saying &quot;We're just doing willworking guys!&quot; does not mesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why they fail to work together worth a damn most of the time. They cannot understand one another and too often cannot abide one another.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T08:30:41-07:00","id":1386410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386235#post1386235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because the books are told from their perspectives, and center on them and their needs and egos. Consider how they appear to the Technocracy, and even to the Disparates.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In the World of Darkness, &quot;bad people&quot; is almost everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The technocracy is an authoritarian organisation who brainwash their agents and everyone they don't like, maintaining them in a permanent state of cognitive dissonance and considering anything not matching their little vision of utopia as terrorist for the crime of existing and justifying their actions throught the work of a convention that is literally based on spreading misinformation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Everyone has an opinion, not all opinion have equal values, and in that scheme, the opinion of the technocracy is worthless.<br /> Especially when everything they accuse the traditions of doing, from wanting to go back to the middle age to terrorism, is demonstrably false.<br /> <br /> As for the Disparates, even those with a past grudge agaisnt the traditions don't consider them evil, but merely misguided.<br /> <br /> <br /> The books are not told from the perspective of the traditions. Most OOC texts are basically positing the 9 as the good guys.<br /> <br /> The guide to the traditions list both good and bad things about the organisation. And terrorism is not part of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the idea that almost everyone is bad people in the WOD, again, it's false.<br /> <br /> Making absolutes about &quot;in the world of darkness, things are that way&quot; doesn't work. The books contradict every of those claims at one point or another.<br /> <br /> The only thing that can be said is that the WOD is slightly darker. Not that 80% of the population is bad enough to be on the hit list of the euthanatos or that heroes doesn't exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T08:33:51-07:00","id":1386411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386218#post1386218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, literal bias. How the Euthanatos select their targets is based in a specific belief system where their definition of bad doesn't mesh with any universal definition of bad. And they don't just kill bad people; they also kill good people for the bad impacts they will have despite their good intentions. The Euthanatos don't have access to the universal naughty and nice list. They're enforcing their morality system on other people violently.<br /> <br /> That said, viewing the Traditions as terrorists or utopians is just looking at the extremes. Most Tradition members are somewhere between the two. Some are attempting to be both extremes at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well, the Euthanatos target serial killers, rapists, abusers in every kind, corrupted officials spreading suffering. Match pretty well universal definitions of bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T08:36:13-07:00","id":1386412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386250#post1386250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never seen the Traditions as people &quot;united to help mankind&quot;. I see them as individuals with private goals who have formed an alliance of convenience in order to stand against a common enemy. That alliance of convenience is a description of both the Council of Nine and each individual Tradition as well.<br /> <br /> And the definition of that alliance can change at any time. At least two Traditions were once members of the Technocracy, and their involvement is only because they became political dissidents within the Union.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That was what they were in the first meeting. Add five centuries and they're no longuer an alliance of conveniance. They built a civilisation together, they are giving birth to &quot;neo traditions&quot;, they have a common goal.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T10:36:37-07:00","id":1386429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the big things that may be influencing my view is the fact that I've never bought into Mage Revised's views that mages don't know that it's all will-working. Dreamspeakers, Hermetics, Technocrats, and so on may all have different tools/foci but they all know how the sausage is made. It's a fight about what tools Sleepers should be presented to use, not a fight over what the nature of awakening is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with this notion, and with any idea that would imply M20 Traditionalists do not believe in their Focus<br /> <br /> But that's neither here nor there for bigotry or infigth. In 2e there was a faction of the Chorus that wanted to get out of the Traditions and refused to believe in unity with heatens. In 2e there was an Etherite faction that was openly misoginistic. Verbena used to forbbide tech.<br /> <br /> Revised Traditions are much more ecumenical than 2e, with all and most believing in their Paradigms. Tolerance it's not founded in the negation of difference, but the acceptance of difference<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Arguably, it makes the Ascension War an even more psychotic waste of lives. </div> </div> </div>Niceties aside, the Ascension War it's not a war about who is rigth or what *is* reality.<br /> It's a war about who gets to rule Earth as immortal god wizards, and who has to go and hidde as a rat.<br /> <br /> Even if all the Masters were of one mind about how magick works, they would still figth because it's the perception of <i>others </i>what ultimately matters in the Consensus. And because there seems to be a net benefit to be gained by making that belief support your agendas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T10:42:37-07:00","id":1386431,"title":"","content":"The Traditions are people with drastically different views of reality with opposing goals and endgames.<br /> Just because they've worked together for a while and played nice with each other isn't indicitive that they truly trust each other. If they ever took down the Technocracy (They won't) then they wouldn't have the cohesion that a common enemy brings and they would go right back to squabbling and fighting amongst themselves with humanity as the group that suffers. The Disparate Alliance is fully aware that each magical group has different, and sometimes diametrically opposed goals, and as such isn't trying to standarize magic or force each other to try and mesh world beliefs together.<br /> Also, while the Technocracy does do bad things as a whole, they are also dealing with extinction level threats and are the only group with /humanity's/ survival in mind. It doesn't excuse their sins, but they technically at war for the future survival of reality. Reality Deviants are very dangerous and its impossible to say the Technocracy hasn't improved the lives of humanity as a whole vastly. To them brainwashing people, including their own people, is literally a safeguard to prevent the world from turning into horror fantasy nightmare that the Traditions could bring about. <br /> Even before the Technocracy existed the awakened were taking advantage of sleepers through magic and megalomania. Yes, some mages treated sleepers with respect and protected them. But many abused their power and caused suffering and pain. The Technocracy is the outcome of such abuse of power. They are trying to give humanity a life of relative peace and stability, give them the gift if ignorance to the evils in the world that they would have no defense against. They gave them tools and weapons that can be used against those evils should they find themselves in situations that could mean life or death.<br /> The Traditions are all about themselves. Believe me, I actually love the Traditions in different ways, but it wouldn't be that farfetched for the Traditions to use the same methods the Technocracy uses if they were in power. In fact I'd personally expect it to come about.<br /> Mages and more specifically magic, by nature, are abusive towards humanity and reality. Hence Paradox and Backlash.<br /> The Technocracy at least tries to be humanity a world were they can thrive, unfortunately they have felt like a drastic set of rules and punishments are needed. Hence why reformation of the Technocracy is probably humanity's best chance at survival the World of Darkness. <br /> I personally think that the Technocracy truly has humanity's best interests at heart but some bad apples have gotten mixed in for purposes of power and also the Nephandi of course.<br /> Also the Traditions habit of trying to force a overarching &quot;culture&quot; among mages as actually quite counterintuitive to mage growth since its just trying to push a belief structure onto everyone and just expect them to adjust their beliefs to what the Traditions want. Yes they'll be able to communicate between them easier, but at the cost of their magical identities. <br /> Thats why I personally like Pillars and Foundations and tend to view Spheres as a metagame mechanic when I do play (Which admittedly isn't often and its been a while since I played with others besides my husband.) I also feel the flexible paradigm system seems more like it would belong to the Disparate Alliance and Orphans. <br /> <br /> Tldr; Traditions are only a thing because of the Technocracy and without it would immediately turn to squabbling and fighting amongst themselves over who's paradigm would be supreme. (You really think each Tradition would give the others their chance for control?)<br /> [That was way longer than I thought it would be ^^; Sorry for the length!]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25226-knightfenrirwulfhart","name":"KnightFenrirWulfhart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T11:44:54-07:00","id":1386443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386429#post1386429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree with this notion, and with any idea that would imply M20 Traditionalists do not believe in their Focus <br /> <br /> But that's neither here nor there for bigotry or infighting. In 2e there was a faction of the Chorus that wanted to get out of the Traditions and refused to believe in unity with heatens. In 2e there was an Etherite faction that was openly misoginistic. Verbena used to forbbide tech.<br /> <br /> Revised Traditions are much more ecumenical than 2e, with all and most believing in their Paradigms. Tolerance it's not founded in the negation of difference, but the acceptance of difference</div> </div> </div> </div>This, with the added caveat that being ecumenical essentially boils down to \u201cthere are a few key points that we can agree on; and in the larger scheme of things, what unites is is more important than what divided us.\u201d That's why I keep harping on the \u201cWe Are All Gods in Disguise\u201d Paradigm from <b>Book of Secrets</b>: while it's not a perfect fit for inclusion in <i>every</i> Traditionist's Focus, something <i>like</i> it <i>should</i> be. <br /> <br /> In particular, I did not intend to imply that Traditionists don't believe in their own Focus; that's literally a contradiction, seeing as how one's Focus is founded on what one believes. No, what I was trying to say is that a Traditionist's Focus that <i>doesn't</i> include some sort of ecumenist Paradigm (such as the aforementioned \u201cWe Are All Gods in Disguise\u201d) isn't representative of the Traditions, just as a Technocratic Focus that doesn't incorporate \u201cTech Holds All Answers\u201d isn't really a Technocratic Focus. <br /> <br /> I would also submit, though, that if you have a mystical Focus (as opposed to a technomantic one), it should be hard for you <i>not</i> to believe in Willworking, as even an Arete 1 Mage is capable of spending the Willpower and accepting the increased difficulty to Work Without Focus \u2014 at least, the way the rules are written. I have a <i>bit</i> of a problem with this, myself, which is why I have a house rule about recasting mystic vs. technomantic as internal vs. external: that way, if your Verbena truly believe that her power comes from the gods that she serves, she has an external Focus and can't Work Without Focus. But that's about as far as I intend to go along that tangent here; the main point is that \u201cI believe in Willworking\u201d isn't the same thing as \u201cI believe that my Practice and Instruments are pointless\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T11:52:04-07:00","id":1386444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386411#post1386411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Euthanatos target serial killers, rapists, abusers in every kind, corrupted officials spreading suffering. Match pretty well universal definitions of bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>They also target children for having the wrong souls.<br /> <br /> The WoD is dark enough that the Euthanatos aren;t flatly condemned as the vigilante religious fanaticism motivated serial killers that they are, because most of the time who they kill are &quot;acceptable targets&quot; to wider mage society (and wider human society), but everyone's suspicious of them because &quot;most&quot; is clearly not &quot;all.&quot; Being Dexter from Dexter makes for compelling characters, but it doesn't actually make them good.<br /> <br /> If the Euthanatos just killed objectively bad people that needed to be killed for the greater good, they wouldn't have one of their core internal laws be a buddy system where you're expected to kill your friend if they cross the line of what the Tradition considers acceptable killing. The core hubris of the Tradition is that they think they can do what they do and be a positive force in the world; despite how frequently they fall into being the exact thing they're supposed to be fighting.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T12:32:37-07:00","id":1386453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386361#post1386361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh....the vast majority of Mages even among the Traditions simply don't realise that its 'will-working' or at least don't agree on what that fundamentally means, the overwhelming bulk of Mages will continue using their Focuses forever and will fundamentally believe in the reality defined by their paradigm til the day they die.<br /> <br /> What needs to be understood is that PCs are not part of that majority and are some of the rare few who possess the ability to grow beyond that if they so choose. Based on the last 20 odd years of play very few even of that number choose to abandon their paradigm and Focus fully.<br /> <br /> Hell, the vast majority of the Masters of the Order of Hermes still use their Focuses even to this day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, totally 100% don't agree with this. It's an idea I've seen online and doesn't make any sense to me. There's a name for these sorts of mages--hedge mages.<br /> <br /> If you don't know will-working is the root, you aren't Awakened. You're using Sorcerer Paths.<br /> <br /> A Foci is a calculator.<br /> <br /> Can you do multiplication without it? Absolutely. It makes it easier. Can you do complicated math without it or even a pen and paper? That's what Arete represents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-07-2020, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T12:44:20-07:00","id":1386459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386444#post1386444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They also target children for having the wrong souls.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Because those would become monsters. Widderslainte are literally &quot;Everything wrong in the world&quot; people reincarnating in the world.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386444#post1386444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the Euthanatos just killed objectively bad people that needed to be killed for the greater good, they wouldn't have one of their core internal laws be a buddy system where you're expected to kill your friend if they cross the line of what the Tradition considers acceptable killing. The core hubris of the Tradition is that they think they can do what they do and be a positive force in the world; despite how frequently they fall into being the exact thing they're supposed to be fighting.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the origin of that practice. The duty of the Euthanatos bring them dangerously close to Jhor taint. It's not hubris, Jhor is a metaphysical taint that have demonstrable effect to mages. That's why they watch each others for search of such taint.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T14:08:50-07:00","id":1386484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386453#post1386453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a name for these sorts of mages--hedge mages.<br /> <br /> If you don't know will-working is the root, you aren't Awakened. You're using Sorcerer Paths.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is explicitly not true in the books. If you don't know that you're toying with the rules of the universe, you're not Awakened. How you conceptualize why you can do that is why paradigm has been a huge deal in the game since the get go. Hedge mages find loopholes in the extant rules of the universe and study how to use them to maximum effect. Awakened mages manifest their own rules.<br /> <br /> Now, I do think that Dataweaver's point is stronger in that the Council of Nine Traditions has fostered enough of a communal cultural that most Tradition mages accept willworking as how magic works on some level. But the Traditions are full of individuals that don't actually buy the Council party line too. As well, the point that what &quot;will-working&quot; even means isn't actually universally agreed on either stands. A Hermetic's indomitable Will giving them power over reality and a Verbena's enforcing the will of their community, are both &quot;will-working,&quot; in vastly different ways, even if they accept that &quot;will&quot; is part of the equation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386459#post1386459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because those would become monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do they know that? As most Time mages would be glad to point out, the future isn't that simple.<br /> <br /> Also, let's remember that they (though it was mutual) murdered children for the crime of... potentially becoming Akashic mages during the Himalayan Wars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Widderslainte are literally &quot;Everything wrong in the world&quot; people reincarnating in the world. </div> </div> </div>Souls and Avatars aren't the same thing.<br /> <br /> And it's not like killing an infant Widderslainte kills the evil part, it just tosses the evil part onto a new kid.<br /> <br /> Senex is presented as quite disappointed with his Tradition with how many of them have given up on actually fixing things, and instead just destroying things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The duty of the Euthanatos bring them dangerously close to Jhor taint. It's not hubris, Jhor is a metaphysical taint that have demonstrable effect to mages. </div> </div> </div>This is... just making my point (also I'll point out the author of Euthanatos Revised's point, he's been pretty clear about it in the past).<br /> <br /> Considering it your duty to do something so bad it metaphysically taints you, and thinking it's a good thing to keep doing it as long as you keep that taint in check, is hubris.<br /> <br /> Jhor is proof of the moral mess Euthanatoic philosophy actually is, and how badly the Tradition needs reformers like Senex to reclaim any sort of moral high ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T14:20:12-07:00","id":1386487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386484#post1386484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> How do they know that? As most Time mages would be glad to point out, the future isn't that simple.<br /> <br /> Also, let's remember that they (though it was mutual) murdered children for the crime of... potentially becoming Akashic mages during the Himalayan Wars.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Except Widderslainte are born evil. They're the kids strangling their twin in the craddle (literal exemple from the book of madness), they're the kids drowning pets and fellow kids because they can. For anyone with Mind, there's a limit to assumption of innocence.<br /> <br /> As for the events of the Himalayan Wars, we can hardly apply real world morals to a war with reincarnating soldiers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386484#post1386484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Souls and Avatars aren't the same thing.<br /> <br /> And it's not like killing an infant Widderslainte kills the evil part, it just tosses the evil part onto a new kid.<br /> <br /> Senex is presented as quite disappointed with his Tradition with how many of them have given up on actually fixing things, and instead just destroying things.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In the Euthanatos paradigm, it's the same thing, and in Meta terms as well, it does not matter if a widderslainte is the soul of the barrabi that entered the caul, the mere presence of the tainted avatar will make it a monster.<br /> <br /> Killing a widderslainte is an act of protection for the family, the people around them, and larger population even if it awaken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386484#post1386484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is... just making my point (also I'll point out the author of Euthanatos Revised's point, he's been pretty clear about it in the past).<br /> <br /> Considering it your duty to do something so bad it metaphysically taints you, and thinking it's a good thing to keep doing it as long as you keep that taint in check, is hubris.<br /> <br /> Jhor is proof of the moral mess Euthanatoic philosophy actually is, and how badly the Tradition needs reformers like Senex to reclaim any sort of moral high ground.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Jhor isn't some moral judgement, you can get jhor from making the Agatha journey into the underworld!<br /> <br /> Jhor is a taint coming from the metaphysical proximity with Death. It's not &quot;murder taint you because it's bad&quot; but &quot;murder taint you because you touch death, repeatedly&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T14:21:40-07:00","id":1386488,"title":"","content":"Mind you, we have Sennex's student in the Mage fiction that I'm blanking on the name of. He went against Euthantatos rules regarding her. She should have been subject to Gilgul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T14:28:33-07:00","id":1386491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386453#post1386453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't know will-working is the root, you aren't Awakened. You're using Sorcerer Paths.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just...wrong, and runs contrary to a good pile of beliefs/practices/paradigms described in M20, along with the concept of instruments and their writeups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T14:30:17-07:00","id":1386493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386488#post1386488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, we have Sennex's student in the Mage fiction that I'm blanking on the name of. He went against Euthantatos rules regarding her. She should have been subject to Gilgul.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Amanda, and one of the book clarify that when Senex killed her previous incarnation, he magically altered her avatar so she would not be reborn as fallen. And indeed, said avatar, which appear multiple times in stories about Amanda, is clearly no longuer a nephandic avatar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T14:30:38-07:00","id":1386494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386491#post1386491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's just...wrong, and runs contrary to a good pile of beliefs/practices/paradigms described in M20, along with the concept of instruments and their writeups.</div> </div> </div> </div>An Awakening is when you understand your will can change reality. If you don't understand that, you can't awaken. You can still do the rituals and go through the motions, though.<br /> <br /> But I admit I'm a 2nd Edition man originally and eventually moved to Revised.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T15:21:35-07:00","id":1386512,"title":"","content":"They're both valid ways of handling the game but I think that we might have boiled down this debate to what is ultimately a difference of paradigm. X D<br /> <br /> Regardless, for my take, I prefer and think it's more interesting to go with the revised philosophy of Awakening. An unlocking of latent potential yes but ultimately one's absolute conviction in their ideals and beliefs that allows them to bend reality and then the journey of self-discovery towards True Ascension where the Willworker must refine their beliefs and consider whether or not what they do is right or even what they think it is. If reality or life or anything is what they think it is.<br /> <br /> I see the merits of running a story in the style of the Awakened all being aware of their ability to harness their Will to shape reality and having the conflict over which method of working will is best, but I ultimately find the personal storytelling potential of the revised philosophy more appealing so that's the one that I lean towards.<br /> <br /> As far as Hedge Magic is concerned, like what others have said above, I generally consider that to be some sort of mystical knack or connection to manipulate existing cosmic mechanisms, mechanisms that the Awakened may or may not be able to create, alter or destroy but mechanisms that can theoretically be learned and used by anyone with the right potential, somewhat akin to the defined and 'linear' magic of most other gamelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T15:39:07-07:00","id":1386514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386487#post1386487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except Widderslainte are born evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>This skips past the &quot;how do they know?&quot; question rather blatantly. How many kids that needed psychological intervention and therapy have the Euthanatoi killed presuming they're a budding Widderslainte? Or just pressuming a budding sociopath because not all kids that show the signs of going down evil paths are Widderslainte?<br /> <br /> You're skipping the whole hubris of all this: the Euthanatos don't have any way to know for sure that a kid is a Widderslainte, or destined to be evil, or whatever. They make educated (sometimes very well educated) attempts to do the best they can, and fill in the doubt that they should have about that with faith in their duty.<br /> <br /> How many mistakes are the Euthanatoi allowed to make before their underlying philosophy comes under question?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the events of the Himalayan Wars, we can hardly apply real world morals to a war with reincarnating soldiers. </div> </div> </div>You're doing it do reincarnating evil Avatars.<br /> <br /> Also, the events of the Himalayan Wars, and specifically that attempts to attack reincarnations is explicitly something that lend to increased damage to the mental state of those Avatars/incarnations. The repeat casualties were noted as increasingly likely to become infernalists or the like as their Avatar's raged against the injustice being done... a direct violation of Euthanatoic philosophy that they did anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the Euthanatos paradigm, it's the same thing, and in Meta terms as well, it does not matter if a widderslainte is the soul of the barrabi that entered the caul, the mere presence of the tainted avatar will make it a monster. </div> </div> </div>It's not really that clear cut.<br /> <br /> And you keep trying to force this to be about Widderslainte. <b>It's not.</b> The Euthanatos don't just kill Nephandi.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Killing a widderslainte is an act of protection for the family, the people around them, and larger population even if it awaken. </div> </div> </div>And it's incredibly short sighted since you know it's going to pop up somewhere else again. If they were really serious about this, they'd capture Widderslainte for Gilgul or get behind Senex's experiments.<br /> <br /> Killing a Widderslainte without any precautions about what happens to that Avatar after is hypocritically short-sighted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Jhor isn't some moral judgement, you can get jhor from making the Agatha journey into the underworld! </div> </div> </div>Repeatedly doing things that taint you with Jhor, knowing the effects Jhor will eventually have on you, is immoral.<br /> <br /> Science and technology aren't inherently moral or immoral. But if you keep inventing guns that are better and better at killing as many people as fast as possible, and do your best to make sure anyone can get their hands on your inventions? There's a moral issue at hand. The Euthanatoi face the same issue. Jhor might not be a moral judgement, but there's only so far you can push willingly exposing yourself to Jhor before you deserve moral judgement for those choices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386488#post1386488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, we have Sennex's student in the Mage fiction that I'm blanking on the name of. He went against Euthantatos rules regarding her. She should have been subject to Gilgul.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386493#post1386493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Amanda, and one of the book clarify that when Senex killed her previous incarnation, he magically altered her avatar so she would not be reborn as fallen. And indeed, said avatar, which appear multiple times in stories about Amanda, is clearly no longuer a nephandic avatar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Senex didn't actually break Euthanatos rules because he killed Mercedes (the Nephandi who Amanda would get her Avatar from). He ran afoul of the Council's rules because the Hermetics wanted Amanda killed as a Widderslainte despite Senex's efforts to cleanse her Avatar between incarnations.<br /> <br /> That said, Senex's success is ultimately left uncertain. Amanda is noted to grow increasingly worried that his efforts only subdued the corruption rather than eliminated it, and that over time she'd eventually fall to her Avatar's true nature. In the Ascension book, she's generally presented as convinced the experiment ultimately failed, and she's on a suicide mission to die before it's too late and she falls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386494#post1386494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Awakening is when you understand your will can change reality. If you don't understand that, you can't awaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, citation please? Because there's a lot of passages in the books over the editions that do not agree with that in the slightest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T15:52:52-07:00","id":1386517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386514#post1386514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, citation please? Because there's a lot of passages in the books over the editions that do not agree with that in the slightest.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you think you Awaken? One of the Son of Ether bits of lore is the Kitab al-Alacir which allows you to awaken because it explains that reality is flexible by willworking.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T16:08:41-07:00","id":1386527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386453#post1386453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, totally 100% don't agree with this. It's an idea I've seen online and doesn't make any sense to me. There's a name for these sorts of mages--hedge mages.<br /> <br /> If you don't know will-working is the root, you aren't Awakened. You're using Sorcerer Paths.<br /> <br /> A Foci is a calculator.<br /> <br /> Can you do multiplication without it? Absolutely. It makes it easier. Can you do complicated math without it or even a pen and paper? That's what Arete represents.</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll it's from Satyros so.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T16:14:37-07:00","id":1386529,"title":"","content":"&quot;No one formula or path can dictate Awakening; this awareness strikes where it will, without distinction.&quot; Mage Revised.<br /> <br /> Mages not truly understanding how Awakenings work is an underlying conceit of the game's logic. If Awakening was truly understood as a process, mages could purposefully Awaken people by forcing them through that process. But since the nature of Awakening is a mystery, it's impossible to reliably cause them.<br /> <br /> Moreover, the books are rather clear that Awakenings are as unique as the individual mage. Every mage experiences Awakening in their own way, from their own perspective, mixed up with their own Avatar.<br /> <br /> Some mages just Awaken. Some mages spend years struggling to figure out what's going on with them as they start to understand things that they shouldn't, and that the weird stuff happening around them is actually because of them. The very fact that some mid-Awakening characters will end up doing Awakened magic despite not having any sort of understanding about their ability to will the universe into compliance undercuts the idea that will is an inherent component instead of just a very powerful tool of magic.<br /> <br /> The Kitab al-Alacir does not describe magic via will-working at all. Everything outside the walls, metaphorically of your mind, are true, you bring them into the walls by exploration, and thus expand yourself if you explore with wisdom, or destroy yourself if you bring in things without properly examining them (aka the Trojan Horse).<br /> <br /> Just as all that talk about Euthanatos philosophy is rooted in their ideal that magic is fueled by duty, not will, the Etherites hold that magic isn't wiling something to exist that doesn't, but finding that with already exists but isn't &quot;within the walls&quot; of other people's minds, and bringing it back with you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T16:18:24-07:00","id":1386531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386529#post1386529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;No one formula or path can dictate Awakening; this awareness strikes where it will, without distinction.&quot; Mage Revised.<br /> <br /> Mages not truly understanding how Awakenings work is an underlying conceit of the game's logic. If Awakening was truly understood as a process, mages could purposefully Awaken people by forcing them through that process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't they? If they couldn't consistently Awaken people then every mage would be an Orphan instead of being like 1% of the Awakened being Orphans. The vast majority are:<br /> <br /> * A Traditionalist grabs a sleeper<br /> * A Traditionalist shows them magic<br /> * The Traditonalist explains their philosophy over several weeks to years<br /> * Sleeper Awakens<br /> * Sleeper joins said Tradition.<br /> <br /> Orphans are:<br /> <br /> * Orphan realizes how reality works on their own and Awakens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T16:21:21-07:00","id":1386532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386517#post1386517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How do you think you Awaken? One of the Son of Ether bits of lore is the Kitab al-Alacir which allows you to awaken because it explains that reality is flexible by willworking.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a citation. <i>This</i> is a citation:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Put simply, a mage is a person with the power to reshape reality through force of will.<br /> <br /> M20 p.19</div>So is this:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Awakening:</b> the state of waking up to one's power to rework reality and perform <i>True Magick</i>.<br /> <br /> M20 p 23</div>And this:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Epiphany:</b> The moment of Awakening; an \u201cAHA!\u201d experience that opens the mage's eyes to new potential.<br /> <br /> M20 p.25</div>It's a subtle thing; but note that neither the entry for Awakening nor the entry for Epiphany makes any reference to will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-11-2020, 02:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T16:25:33-07:00","id":1386535,"title":"","content":"Okay, I'm going to concede the argument because I don't want to go through the books for specific references. I appreciate you taking the time to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T16:31:14-07:00","id":1386538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386494#post1386494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An Awakening is when you understand your will can change reality. If you don't understand that, you can't awaken. You can still do the rituals and go through the motions, though.<br /> <br /> But I admit I'm a 2nd Edition man originally and eventually moved to Revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am a Sorcerers Crusade person that upgraded to M20 (loving it), and have been collecting revised and other material to use as kindling. No, I am not starting an actua fire. I am running an M20 game, and though my philosophy says that previous edition material may be disregarded at will, I want to use it as fuel for ideas and backstory.<br /> <br /> Anyway...<br /> My understanding of Focus is mostly based on M20. And nowhere (that I see) does it suggest that Mages think they are merely working will. Focus = Paradigm + Practice + Instruments. You may be able to transcend Instruments, but you can never outgrow Paradigm or Practice. The closed I can imagine that mages imagine they are working will, is the idea that by will one is setting forces into motion. I am not creating lightning by will. My will is what is causing a &quot;connecting of the wires&quot; between the world of Platonic Forms and the world we perceive. That is a Hermetic way of looking at it.<br /> Now, we as players know that it is all in their heads. All the rituals and ingredients are meaningless. *We* know that, but the characters cannot comprehend it.<br /> <br /> Definitions need to be clarified. If you are working from M2 or Mr, I do think the word Focus is n mere reference to Ritual Tools (SC) or Instruments (M20). The way it works now is that you only get ONE Focus. The cornerstone of that Focus is Paradigm. Paradigm manifests through Practice, and Practices are conducted with Instruments. I know I am repeating myself, but there seems to be a contradiction of ideas stemming from working from different editions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T22:42:43-07:00","id":1386616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions#post1385487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some fans overcompensate by saying, &quot;The Traditions are actually a bunch of people fighting against toilets, lights, and vaccines! They're a bunch of Luddite terrorists!&quot;<br /> <br /> This is completely irreconcilable with the way they're presented. They are a collection of Buddhists, Mad Scientists, Christians, Thuggee, and Witches who are all united by their desire to help mankind. If they can overcome that, they're not going to sweat indoor plumbing.</div> </div> </div> </div>So. Here's the thing about this. The point isn't that they're actively against toilets, lights, and vaccines. It's that they want to tear down the framework that allows for toilets, lights, and vaccines in order to allow for magic to be freely used.<br /> <br /> Toilets, lights, vaccines. They all work because people believe that the world works on the simple rules of science. You do something, you get this result. Every time, every place, no moon phases, no ritualism, just simple physical processes.<br /> <br /> Now, the Traditions might SAY they're not against Toilets, lights, and vaccines. But they're certainly willing to toss them in the path of the bus to get their way. Could be they're right. Could be technology can survive the technocratic paradigm being shattered. But that's not a sure bet, and is even backed up by the fact that in canon, technology tends to break down more frequently outside of technocratic paradigm zones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T23:30:12-07:00","id":1386626,"title":"","content":"I'd say, with regards to playing a member of the Traditions, the game would be about gaining enough power and wisdom and influence within the Traditions fast enough to take the reigns of Tradition power before someone bad for humanity does and then figuring out a way to preserve the treasures of the past,bring magick and wonder to the world, and save the world from destruction despite a better adjusted and equipped foe wh actually means well, despite more insidious enemies who have infiltrated the traditions and the aforementioned foe, and despite the Tradition's own failings. It's not about destroying all the good that technology brings but about averting the bad that misuse of any form of power can bring, be it technlogical advancement, eldrich evil, or one's own powerful magick. It's about maneuvering through gray areas, making questionable choices by choosing the best among bad choices, and trying to avoid civilian casualties in a world gone insane. <br /> <br /> While well meaning in principle, without the Traditions as a counterbalance, the Technocracy might have already turned all of humanity into a giant machine enslaved to a powerful superhuman intelligence, after all. This is much the same way the Traditions might have done something similar under the leadership of Solificati. Now, with the old leaders of Traditions gone, a dedicated group of players can play the guys who actually turn things around for the Traditions... or they can find out why there's no easy way to fix the woes of the world. The same goes for the Technocracy, despite all its resources, power, and ideals, the good people in it, and the good its done for a lot, it can still commit atrocities, potentially end the world, or transform the world into a living hell in the name of safety and order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T00:18:32-07:00","id":1386629,"title":"","content":"It's an interesting point because this wouldn't be an issue for me pre-Revised. I have no problem believing the Masters were against plumbing, vaccines, and so on. They're the kind of people who I fully believe would want to get rid of colonists centuries latter or restore Mythical China if it means eradicating civilization. However, I thought one of the major points of Revised was the fact that the Masters were all killed. It was a massive boon for the Technocracy as it eliminated the worst of their organization (people alive when eugenics, racial slavery, and &quot;White Man's Burden&quot; were all the rage) while leaving room for new ones to take over.<br /> <br /> I guess I always assumed the same would happen for Traditions post-Avatar Storm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T00:57:20-07:00","id":1386636,"title":"","content":"Most time I've seen Tradition characters RPed, they indeed were not against plumbing, vaccines and the like.<br /> The books point this out, too - they were previously normal people with normal lives, a job and modern comforts - and once they awakened, they didn't shift from that standpoint of 'these everyday essentials are absolutely okay' much. It *is* safe to say that most members of the Traditions these days don't want to go back to the dark ages - <i>and even if they want to replace certain technologies, they want good alternatives first</i>.<br /> <br /> But there are always exceptions, even among new members.<br /> <br /> From what is written and I've seen RPed though, yeah, 'back to the dark ages' it's not really the norm. That said, each faction has its radical elements, new and old, of course.<br /> <br /> <br /> The point of Enginseer-42 kind of also stands - *if* a technology only works because classic Magic is not working, *then* things get a bit problematic.<br /> But really, these days people (even if mythic magic became part of the consensus) would have no trouble combining <i>'Pressure pushes water through the plumbing'</i> with an understanding of classical mythic Magic. So I don't think sanitary installations are at risk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 05-08-2020, 04:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T00:58:59-07:00","id":1386638,"title":"","content":"Also, if the Traditions were about destroying belief in technology, I don't think they would have let the Virtual Adepts or Son's of Ether in. They're more against the idea of a consensus that sees only one way to do things. Otherwise they'd have been actively working to stop technological progress more directly, I reckon. Instead they pick up on technology and improve on it with magic a lot, probably trying to create a world in which both coexist... Historically speaking, the Hermetics used to be the tyrants in power though, but that's kinda gone now with the whole Avatar storm bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 05-08-2020, 04:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T01:15:18-07:00","id":1386640,"title":"","content":"The way it was taught to me was ,ignoring the part where the Technocracy tends towards killing mages who aren't part of it, Traditions have two issues with the way the Technocracy has been running the Paradihm.First, that's its boring. Here meaning there is no room in the Paradigm of the Technocratic Union for things that don't align with it. Most notable I believe would be that bit on how the Sons of Aether left because Aether was excised from the Paradigm when that was basically the only rule the Sons had. The second is less kind. Essentially the Traditions are of the opinion that their way is the best path of enlightment for the world to follow. In this scenario any particular tradition has less issue with what the Technocracy has done so much as they object to the fact that its not them in the Technocracy's seat.<br /> <br /> That's on a larger scale though. I figure on the lower scale most tradition mages ,again ignoring the marked for termination reality deviant title, probably just view it as a way to expand the world and better oneself and the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T01:46:57-07:00","id":1386643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386636#post1386636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most time I've seen Tradition characters RPed, they indeed were not against plumbing, vaccines and the like.<br /> The books point this out, too - they were previously normal people with normal lives, a job and modern comforts - and once they awakened, they didn't shift from that standpoint of 'these everyday essentials are absolutely okay' much. It *is* safe to say that most members of the Traditions these days don't want to go back to the dark ages - <i>and even if they want to replace certain technologies, they want good alternatives first</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct, its something posted a lot on line but its made up whole cloth and bears no resemblance to anything thats ever appeared in a book even during 1st Edition. Its basically a giant self perpetuating strawman fallacy that for some reason won't die like it should.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T02:14:12-07:00","id":1386647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386643#post1386643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are correct, its something posted a lot on line but its made up whole cloth and bears no resemblance to anything thats ever appeared in a book even during 1st Edition. Its basically a giant self perpetuating strawman fallacy that for some reason won't die like it should.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, Voormas wants to destroy everything but he's as close to a Nephandi as a non-Nephandi can get really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T02:37:43-07:00","id":1386654,"title":"","content":"Additionally, science and technology predated the Order of Reason rather significantly. The Mythic Ages the Traditions love to gush over were still full of mundane technology built from mundane proto-scientific experimentation... because the Tradition world view has never been &quot;technology bad,&quot; but that, &quot;magic is supposed to be better than mundane technology.&quot;<br /> <br /> The early mages weren't killing blacksmiths for constantly trying to make a better sword, they were taking superior craftsmanship in swords and then enchanting them for swords no Sleeper could match. They weren't stopping the Greeks during their explosion of invention, or the early Chinese innovations in mass production, or all the groups that independently figured out terrace farming, etc. They didn't complain about Roman public toilets and sewer systems, or cement that took oh so long to recreate after the recipe was lost. They didn't have a problem with the Islamic Golden Age where modern science first started to come into a shape we recognize. Etc.etc. etc.<br /> <br /> For the vast majority of history, mages and technology and science all got along. The Tradition (and notably plenty of the Crafts/Disparates as well) tilt against those things is a direct response to the Order of Reason and then the Technocracy turning them into weapons in the Ascension War, rather than leaving them to be how Sleepers did things. And that tilt has largely corrected itself by the &quot;now&quot; of the setting because of the weight of all the mages having grown up in modern times.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> Edit: And Voormas doesn't actually give a shit about technology or anything. He's a coward that doesn't want to die, so he's going to do whatever it takes to kill death itself, and damn the consequences. Given the state of the WoD, a Nephandi that just wants to destroy everything is morally less horrible than Voormas wouldn't make so many bad things impossible to kill, and everyone else not even capable of dying to end it all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 05-08-2020, 05:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T08:17:54-07:00","id":1386696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386643#post1386643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are correct, its something posted a lot on line but its made up whole cloth and bears no resemblance to anything thats ever appeared in a book even during 1st Edition. Its basically a giant self perpetuating strawman fallacy that for some reason won't die like it should.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The concept comes from the Guide to the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> It's literally propaganda and disinformation.<br /> <br /> That's the issue with this forum. It seems a lot of people takes the Convention revised and guide to the technocracy as god's words on the world of mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T08:26:05-07:00","id":1386699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386696#post1386696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the issue with this forum. It seems a lot of people takes the Convention revised and guide to the technocracy as god's words on the world of mage.</div> </div> </div> </div> I've never encountered that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T08:43:52-07:00","id":1386704,"title":"","content":"As <i>Enginseer-42 </i>said, it's true that in M20 (and sometimes elsewhere) it's suggested that tech works bad (or not at all) if the Paradigm doesn't support it, however it's also implied that mundane tech only trully stops working in the most remote areas of the Earth. Or in specific Umbral landscapes. Places like that can reasonably be said to be outside of what Traditional <b>ideal </b>&quot;terraforming&quot; does.<br /> <br /> Much more representative of the state of science and technology in a victory of the Traditions it's what they did in Horizon. Mages rule, people have phones and flying carpets...but they also have man-eating dragons.<br /> <br /> It's also possible that the traditions will fall on infigthing after winning. In that case the ideal will never come to pass, and then the future of the technology it's going to be much more up for grabs. But much of it it's going to depend on the will of people (as no Tradition will grab the whole of the Consensus), and I think most people wants their tech to work<br /> <br /> I don't think current tech will stop working. Then again, as <i>Ambrosia</i> said, one can't be 100% sure <hr /><br /> It's my impression that the debate Technocracy/Traditions it's akin to the debate between &quot;freedom&quot; and &quot;security&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Traditions, ideally (a lot of members fall short from these ideals), want people to have the potential to Awaken, and then freedom to explore every elegible path to become better.<br /> <br /> In a sense, the Traditions are a bit like a nicer, softer, version of the more philosophical <b>Sith</b>. They could say that th Techncoracy &quot;robs people of their victories&quot; (yeah, they do, as proven each time they congratulate themselves for flush toilets :P ) Technocracy dulls humanity, making them ignorant &quot;for their own good&quot;, preventing them (and wizards) from freely pursuing the birthrigth of humanity: magick.<br /> <br /> This is an ideal that resonates strongly with mystic wizards that are being opressed by the Technocracy, because it implies that they will be free to practice and share their arts, becoming as powerful as they want. It also resonates with the elitist VA, and the no less elitist Etherites - both believe in a world free of pesky corporate limitations to one's genius.<br /> <br /> However, these ideas often neglect the well being of the common man, the one that's not going to &quot;git gud&quot; any time soon.<br /> <br /> For instance, let's remember that Traditional ideas about promoting *wonder* and *magick* include magnificent man-eating dragons roaming the land once more. Now, monsters aren't likely to overrun humanity (surely not if wizards have a say about this), but they won't have Unbelief pushing them to the antipodes of the world if the Trads have their way.<br /> <br /> Now, that's not to say the Traditions don't care about sleepers. The Traditions have a law about protecting sleepers, often put humanity first, and are *constantly* figthing themselves and others for moral reasons. Like Extatics that violate the code of Ananda, or Euthanatos that violate the Chodona - we often see how these are brutally punished by their own factions. But that just highligths their darker aspects. Even the most idealistic often will favor their esoteric morals over the banal ideals of the uninitiated (the Technocracy it's also guilty of this).<br /> <br /> And that's before mentioning that they often *fail* to \u00b4police thier own because of how fragmented they are - maybe this could chage if they weren't the underdogs, but there's no guarantee. It's quite likely that a lot of people one could only characterize as &quot;evil wizards&quot; are going to have it a lot easier under Traditional ruling - rules about protecting sleepers notwithstanding. Let's remember here that many Tradition mages still remember Mistridge as the offense that ignited the war, w/o reflecting much if they had it coming<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> One has to remember that Alice's wonderland was a pretty dark place...and one has to start questioning how far this freedom of magick and wonder can be taken before one starts begging for protection. That's where I think you can find the darkness within the Traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-08-2020, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T08:45:48-07:00","id":1386705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386699#post1386699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I've never encountered that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's in every conversation about Technocracy vs Traditions.<br /> <br /> &quot;the traditions wants to end toilets, lights and automobiles!&quot; is something that always come forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member"