r421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T11:23:25-07:00","id":1386743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386718#post1386718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And very quickly gets shot down whenever it does.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And yet it come back again and again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T12:37:19-07:00","id":1386756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386743#post1386743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And yet it come back again and again.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's undead!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T12:43:48-07:00","id":1386758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386704#post1386704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a sense, the Traditions are a bit like a nicer, softer, version of the more philosophical <b>Sith</b>. They could say that th Techncoracy &quot;robs people of their victories&quot; (yeah, they do, as proven each time they congratulate themselves for flush toilets :P ) Technocracy dulls humanity, making them ignorant &quot;for their own good&quot;, preventing them (and wizards) from freely pursuing the birthrigth of humanity: magick.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's sort of a Space Whale Aesop really but one objectively true in the setting.<br /> <br /> Every person who dies of cancer, today, could be cured by someone with sufficient bone-waving and sorcery. You can make an analogy to real-life hucksterism but that's objectively not true in Mage: The Ascension.<br /> <br /> Which means that the Technocracy suppresses real life discoveries and &quot;science&quot; in order to keep their own as the only game in town.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T13:12:31-07:00","id":1386770,"title":"","content":"Regarding magic vs. science... I made both my Tradition and Technocrat players deeply uncomfortable when a time traveler from 1000 years in the future \u201caccidentally\u201d mentioned that the dominant magical organization of the future was the \u201cNew World Order of Hermes.\u201d<br /> <br /> I tend to fall into the \u201cMage is the lightest shaded section of the World of Darkness\u201d camp. It\u2019s not meant to play like Vampire or Werewolf and a big chunk of its appeal is that it doesn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> If every game played and felt just like D&amp;D, why bother with anything but D&amp;D. If you want bleak and hopeless you play Vampire*. If you want bleak and hopeless with a side of ridiculously large dice pools and depictions of violence you play Werewolf. If you you want downright nihilism there\u2019s Wraith.<br /> <br /> Mage is what you play because you want to experience what I call \u201cThe Dark Fantastic.\u201d The world is dark and dangerous... but at the same time full of wonder and a chance to \u2018earn your happy ending.\u2019<br /> <br /> In that respect, the mixed (but mostly okay) bag that is the Traditions makes sense. It has problems, but there enough there that you can generally root for the faction. Particularly the younger generations the PCs are intended to be members of.<br /> <br /> Yes, you can tell a heroic tale of the Technocracy too, but that\u2019s mainly because the rank and file aren\u2019t the same as the leadership and there are far darker villains in the setting for them to fight (i.e. it\u2019s okay to root for Magneto when he\u2019s fighting the Red Skull).<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I see the future of Mage not as some Armageddon (the term foisted on it by Revised to bring it line with Gehenna/Apocalypse), but, as I hinted at in my open, the less extreme members of the Traditions and Technocracy finding a middle ground that balances safety vs. wonder.<br /> <br /> Or as I\u2019ve joked about the eventual peace treaty... \u201cOkay, we\u2019ll give you dragons, but they\u2019re limited to dog size and eat only fish. In exchange we get our cybernetic wi-fi access and cold fusion technology.\u201d<br /> <br /> * Vampire is kinda weird for me on the bleakness scale because I\u2019ve always considered the \u201cWormwood\u201d ending in Gehenna as the canonical one for the line.<br /> <br /> Further, the main time I ran it I threw in the \u201cdying old homeless man outside the sanctuary\u201d option just before the final sunrise (and since the old church had no power, no one had any charged phones after 40 days). As should shock no one... only those PCs willing to sacrifice all their struggles to survive by going out to help someone the world didn\u2019t care about and would be dead soon either way... only those actually passed the test.<br /> <br /> Only one did... the others saluted his sacrifice and were still just inside the doors when the whole place blew apart and exposed everyone to the sunrise. Cue surprise as the player who thought he was getting a heroic sacrifice instead becomes human and everyone else burned to ash.<br /> <br /> Throw in the final blessing (in this case by the old man who then disappeared without a trace) on the now human PC and his descendants and the PC and the Dhampir** girl (the only other survivor) walking off into the sunrise and it\u2019s hard not to feel like the reason for the Darkness isn\u2019t nihilism, but contrast.<br /> <br /> ** also contrasting the darkness... the last generations produced mortal children. Children who could have children of their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T14:03:53-07:00","id":1386775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386758#post1386758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's sort of a Space Whale Aesop really but one objectively true in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in Troper terms, Mage's issue is that it's heavily into the Fantastic Aesop (where the Aesop is valid, but only within the setting and thus struggles to be applied to real life) instead of the Space Whale Aesop (where the Aesop is valid, but relies on possible actions with highly improbable from the perspective of 'now' consequences that it gets weird).<br /> <br /> While we know that Star Trek VI's message is pro-environmentalism and specifically preserving endangered species, saving the whales because in the distant future aliens thinking that whales are the form of life on Earth worth talking to will show up on kill humanity because they don't have whales to talk to is... a bit of a reach.<br /> <br /> Stamping out mysticism is bad because mystics can cure cancer isn't much of a reach, but is a problem because mystics can only cure cancer in the fantasy rules of Mage.<br /> <br /> Mage's morals can feel very disconnected, but a lot of that is also that progressive-libertarianism isn't terribly common as a political ideology (or at least openly identified with). Most real world progressives have a stronger collectivist bend that's at odds with the Tradition's view of how to achieve pluralism through individualism. Most real world libertarians have a strong conservative or at least laissez faire feeling towards even liking the idea of pluralism, putting them at odds with the Traditions' progressive streak despite promoting a more individualist stance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T14:39:41-07:00","id":1386780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386775#post1386775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage's morals can feel very disconnected, but a lot of that is also that progressive-libertarianism isn't terribly common as a political ideology (or at least openly identified with). Most real world progressives have a stronger collectivist bend that's at odds with the Tradition's view of how to achieve pluralism through individualism. Most real world libertarians have a strong conservative or at least laissez faire feeling towards even liking the idea of pluralism, putting them at odds with the Traditions' progressive streak despite promoting a more individualist stance.</div> </div> </div> </div>You hit on what has always been the weirdest element of the Traditions that also applies to the Technocrats in that they're fascist social progressives. Militant authoritarian cult of personality-dominated individuals against individual rights but against racism, poverty, and systematic abuses against anyone but supernaturals.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I feel like the only thing I ever saw similar was the Templars vs. Assassins in the AC games when they still were heavy on metaplot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T20:28:03-07:00","id":1386891,"title":"","content":"My opinion is that the Technocracy is very regimented, so any atrocities it commits are based on orders from above. The more liberated philosophy of the Traditions means that dubious things they do are more likely to be the result of individual members or sub-groups acting on their own. That gives the Traditions more of an ability to deny culpability when they want to do so, but not necessarily a better record overall.<br /> <br /> That's not really based on knowledge of the setting, though. It's just the way I would play it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T21:55:22-07:00","id":1386905,"title":"","content":"It is fairly accurate. Because of the Union's structure, it's hard to avoid the damage it does being rooted in the organization itself, while the Traditions' decentralized nature makes blame easier to pin on smaller groups.<br /> <br /> I compared the Traditions to NATO earlier, and it applies to this sort of thing. The rest of NATO doesn't generally get much, or any, flak when the US does really sketchy stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T22:12:19-07:00","id":1386909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386758#post1386758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's sort of a Space Whale Aesop really but one objectively true in the setting.<br /> <br /> Every person who dies of cancer, today, could be cured by someone with sufficient bone-waving and sorcery. You can make an analogy to real-life hucksterism but that's objectively not true in Mage: The Ascension.<br /> <br /> Which means that the Technocracy suppresses real life discoveries and &quot;science&quot; in order to keep their own as the only game in town.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that is not actually true in game since the World of Darkness is supposed to mirror our world. Cancer was not something that suddenly appeared once the Order of Reason/Technocratic Union got control. When all of the Traditions could do everything without fear, cancer was out there not being cured en masse. And all sorts of other diseases causing huge infant mortality rates, lowered life expectations, and terrible pandemics killing millions every so often.<br /> <br /> Instead, the Technocrats introduced a paradigm that produced sanitation, vaccines, and antibiotics and wiped out a lot of diseases. So obviously they aren't holding back humanity in terms of disease. They've dramatically advanced it. If the Traditions could produce a healthier world, you'd have to explain why they didn't do it.<br /> <br /> When it comes to things like cancer, both the Traditions and Technocracy have super sorcery/science that could cure INDIVIDUAL patients with otherwise incurable diseases. And they seem to apply that in singular cases.<br /> <br /> On a purely materialistic perspective, the Technocracy wins hands down in terms of benefiting the world. Their downside is that they are becoming increasingly authoritarian and some of their dictates are becoming arbitrary. They're also so mechanistic that they are denying humanity's spiritual side and effectively grinding people down to hopelessness. They're seeking control for the purpose of control, not to better the world. Hence why the Etherites and Virtual Adepts defected. It's an issue of freedom versus security, and currently the Traditions are on the side of freedom because they're on the outs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T22:26:34-07:00","id":1386912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386909#post1386909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that is not actually true in game since the World of Darkness is supposed to mirror our world. Cancer was not something that suddenly appeared once the Order of Reason/Technocratic Union got control. When all of the Traditions could do everything without fear, cancer was out there not being cured en masse. And all sorts of other diseases causing huge infant mortality rates, lowered life expectations, and terrible pandemics killing millions every so often.</div> </div> </div> </div>*snip*<br /> <br /> At the risk of interrupting your statement, that's the premise of the game. If you reject the idea that if people clapped their hands together and can cure cancer then you reject the game's premise. Because the Traditions are not trying to kill babies. They want to help babies. Because their way works equally well. Which is part of why so many scientific minded geeks have an issue with the game's premise. But the Traditions are right and are not anti-science. Because science (i.e. a factual study of the world) in this world says this works.<br /> <br /> As corrected earlier, it's a Fantastic Aesop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-09-2020, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T22:34:11-07:00","id":1386915,"title":"","content":"To play sorcerer's advocate for a moment.<br /> <br /> Assuming that in the pre-Order of Reason World of Darkness there was still diseases and illnesses propagated in the way that conventional medical science understands, which given Consensual Reality is something that could be debated.<br /> <br /> In pre-OoR society, they recognized that people from time to time would grow sick and suffer and perhaps even die, so they would do their level best to treat them. Whether through trying to expel spirits, using folk medicine, meditation, prayer, alchemical cleansing, arcane ritual, or whatever zaniness your local medical doctor etherite has cooked up.<br /> <br /> The important thing to note is that in the context of the World of Darkness and the paradigm prior to the Order of Reason, these medical practices aren't entirely limited to Willworkers. Certainly the Awakened excelled but when Consensual Reality called for spirit medicine or alchemical purification or sympathetic prayer; those were the tools of the day. Doctors could heal through appeasing spirits, cleaning the body, or calling for divine intercession.<br /> <br /> The doctors of that time might not have called things what we call them today, but they recognized when people suffered and would become sick and if they recognized the nature of the suffering they would use what had been sometime prior been found to work in healing it. <br /> <br /> Of course, as people have noted before, taking the implications of Consensual Reality into account leads to some bizarre and unhelpful allegories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T22:38:56-07:00","id":1386916,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I have run House Rule games on these premises in some Chronicles:<br /> <br /> * The Technocracy is not responsible for science. They only use science as a way to work coincidental magic and promote it so they can work coincidental magic.<br /> * Science works entirely normally.<br /> * The Technocracy want to wipe out other mage groups so they have a monopoly on magic so they can control the world from behind the scenes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T00:54:43-07:00","id":1386928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386912#post1386912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you reject the idea that if people clapped their hands together and can cure cancer then you reject the game's premise.</div> </div> </div> </div>You didn't understand my comment so I will try again. I am not disputing that some highly skilled members of the Traditions can cure cancer. I even said that in my response when I said that both sides could obviously cure &quot;incurable&quot; diseases..<br /> <br /> It's just that in the setting, the Traditions OBVIOUSLY DON'T BOTHER TO DO SO ON A MASS SCALE. And it's not because the Technocracy is blocking them. Because before the Technocracy rose to power, the Traditions didn't do anything like that. So you must acknowledge the Traditions (in their original forms) didn't even care enough to do so. So they obviously don't want to &quot;help babies&quot; any more than the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> So you can't claim some kind of moral superiority of the Traditions based on something both they and the Technocracy do.<br /> <br /> So I'm not disputing that their way is just as valid as the Technocracy's. It's that they too &quot;suppress&quot; their &quot;discoveries&quot; and &quot;magic&quot; ... for whatever screwed up reason they have. Unlike the Technocracy who ostensibly allowed sanitation, vaccines, and antibiotics to work and improve health on a mass scale, the Traditions never even bothered to try. So in a real way, the Technocracy does want to help babies more than the Traditions do. Because they actually did.<br /> <br /> Of course, maybe you are arguing that cancer and disease didn't actually exist when the Traditions were &quot;in charge&quot;. But I don't think you are. That would create huge problems for the setting if the World of Darkness diverged so incredibly from the real world.<br /> <br /> A likely Mage explanation is that doing something like curing cancer and other diseases en masse unleashes some terrible Paradox effect which is why nobody does it. Of course, that still leaves the Technocracy a giant win because they figured out how to drive the mortality rates down anyway when the Traditions didn't.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T00:56:45-07:00","id":1386929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386916#post1386916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I have run House Rule games on these premises in some Chronicles:<br /> <br /> * The Technocracy is not responsible for science. They only use science as a way to work coincidental magic and promote it so they can work coincidental magic.<br /> * Science works entirely normally.<br /> * The Technocracy want to wipe out other mage groups so they have a monopoly on magic so they can control the world from behind the scenes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only thing wrong with this post... is calling any of these house rules.<br /> <br /> The first and third are explicitly true.<br /> <br /> The second is true, though complicated since mundane science can't work entirely normally, even if it can work close enough to normal that Sleepers aren't going to notice.<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> <br /> <br /> The Technocracy didn't create a paradigm that allows those things to exist. Sanitation, vaccines, and antibiotics (or at least similar to willow bark tea vs. aspirin), are things that predate the Technocracy by thousands of years.<br /> <br /> What the Order of Reason and then Technocracy did, was push a mix of mass production, and Reality Zone manipulation that made it easier to turn Awakening magic into mundane technology as long as it abides OoR/Union rules.<br /> <br /> This was <i>awalys</i> about uses the masses. The OoR gave Sleepers power, so the OoR could take control of the great power of being able to dictate the Reality Zone of the material plane as a whole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because before the Technocracy rose to power, the Traditions didn't do anything like that. </div> </div> </div>Before the OoR rose to power, the Traditions didn't exist. Most mages were isolated in small groups, and didn't have the infrastructure to do anything on a mass scale. The Traditions were never in power. The groups that would join up into the Traditions were local powers.<br /> <br /> Yes, they didn't put a lot of energy into making human life as comfortable as possible, but that's actually really hard for a dozen or so mages to do for a very large amount of normal folks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 05-09-2020, 04:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T01:26:32-07:00","id":1386932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386928#post1386928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You didn't understand my comment so I will try again. I am not disputing that some highly skilled members of the Traditions can cure cancer. I even said that in my response when I said that both sides could obviously cure &quot;incurable&quot; diseases..<br /> <br /> It's just that in the setting, the Traditions OBVIOUSLY DON'T BOTHER TO DO SO ON A MASS SCALE. And it's not because the Technocracy is blocking them. Because before the Technocracy rose to power, the Traditions didn't do anything like that. So you must acknowledge the Traditions (in their original forms) didn't even care enough to do so. So they obviously don't want to &quot;help babies&quot; any more than the Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>That gets into crypto-history but if there's a Mythic Age of the World of Darkness wouldn't they have actually created a China that had things like dragons, alchemical immortality, and armies of clay warriors? Plus, wouldn't prayer actually have healed people in the Middle Ages? Because once we start down this rabbit hole, we start getting the fact that the history of magick in the WOD isn't the history of our world.<br /> <br /> Then we also question, &quot;Wait, the Technocracy didn't exist until the 14th century, doesn't that mean the Order of Hermes created running water and indoor plumbing in Rome?&quot;<br /> <br /> Because large organized civilizations existed before the Union's ideals for one. Does that mean the Traditions made them or at least their ancestors?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T02:54:01-07:00","id":1386938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386916#post1386916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I have run House Rule games on these premises in some Chronicles:<br /> <br /> * The Technocracy is not responsible for science. They only use science as a way to work coincidental magic and promote it so they can work coincidental magic.<br /> * Science works entirely normally.<br /> * The Technocracy want to wipe out other mage groups so they have a monopoly on magic so they can control the world from behind the scenes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Uh...none of those are House Rules they are explicitly how it works in vanilla Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T05:36:42-07:00","id":1386960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386932#post1386932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That gets into crypto-history but if there's a Mythic Age of the World of Darkness wouldn't they have actually created a China that had things like dragons, alchemical immortality, and armies of clay warriors? Plus, wouldn't prayer actually have healed people in the Middle Ages? Because once we start down this rabbit hole, we start getting the fact that the history of magick in the WOD isn't the history of our world.<br /> <br /> Then we also question, &quot;Wait, the Technocracy didn't exist until the 14th century, doesn't that mean the Order of Hermes created running water and indoor plumbing in Rome?&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's the eternal consistency issue of MtA, it's two premises, that it's story match ours and the other that reality is bent by belief contradict each other.<br /> <br /> Just in the modern era, evangelists gathering religious folks to pray away hurricanes would actually have a chance to work, antivaxers would have no health issue using &quot;alternate medicine&quot;, &quot;detoxination&quot; techniques or any of theses, exorcists would heal mentally ill people, who would have been possessed all along,etc...<br /> <br /> And that's not talking about the way science would work in such universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T08:04:29-07:00","id":1386975,"title":"","content":"It does, however, point out one of the potential differences between what the Technocracy does and what everyone else does: the Technocracy eventually gets its innovations into the hands of ordinary citizens. That is, after sufficient \u201cterranorming\u201d (if I'm understanding the term right), things that started out as Inventions that only Enlightened Scientists could use can eventually end up as common, everyday fixtures in everyone's household. While theoretically the Traditions <i>could</i> replicate this feat, in practice they don't: if you want to benefit from faith healing, you have to rely on the generosity of a faith healer. <br /> <br /> To the extent that the Traditions care about the common man, it's largely in reaction to the Technocracy's very real inroads in that regard. But absent that reaction, Tradition goals tend to focus more on empowering the mage, with the Sleepers benefitting from a sort of \u201ctrickle down effect\u201d: if mages are empowered, then the communities that they favor will benefit from that: if the master does well, so will his servants. In contrast, the Technocracy tends to try to empower the Masses directly (or at least they did, until they went off the rails). <br /> <br /> And while the Technocracy isn't responsible for any technology prior to their appearance in the mid-19th century, they weren't the first Enlightened Scientists in the setting. Heck, even the Conventions of the original Order of Reason didn't pop up out of nowhere in the 1300s: the likes of the Artificers were around long before the Craftmasons recruited them to their cause. You can't credit indoor plumbing to the Technocracy or even to the Order or Reason; but it may well have been something that an Artificer came up with long ago. And in China, the history of the Technocrats goes back thousands of years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T09:33:51-07:00","id":1386990,"title":"","content":"Also worth noting in regards to the science vs. magic split is that, before they founded the Order of Reason, the Craftsmasons were members of the Order of Hermes\u2019 House ex Miscellanea (one of the reasons Clan Tremere always has influence over various Mason organizations in my Vampire-exclusive games... ever wonder why they do so many blood drives?).<br /> <br /> The Craftsmasons decided they wanted to democratize magic by pushing a paradigm that allowed for repeatable results independent of the user. During the Sorcerer\u2019s Crusade period c. 1450 many of their devices were subject to Paradox, but they took their lumps from it and kept pushing little by little to get technology anyone could use into the collective beliefs of humanity.<br /> <br /> Also worth noting is that the Craftsmasons were purged when the Order of Reason was reformed by the same sort of elitists who believed they had a divine right to rule... only now they would rule over the masses via their mastery of technology. <br /> <br /> The Technocrats cut out the soul of the Order (\u201cmake the common man the equal of mages\u201d) in the name of power (\u201cthe common man is too ignorant to rule himself, we must use our technology to control him for his own good\u201d).<br /> <br /> I find the Technocracy can best be explained by a C. S. Lewis quote;<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cOf all tyrannies, a tyranny sincerely exercised for the good of its victims may be the most oppressive. It would be better to live under robber barons than under omnipotent moral busybodies. The robber baron's cruelty may sometimes sleep, his cupidity may at some point be satiated; but those who torment us for our own good will torment us without end for they do so with the approval of their own conscience.<br /> <br /> \u201cThey may be more likely to go to Heaven yet at the same time likelier to make a Hell of earth. This very kindness stings with intolerable insult. To be &quot;cured&quot; against one's will and cured of states which we may not regard as disease is to be put on a level of those who have not yet reached the age of reason or those who never will; to be classed with infants, imbeciles, and domestic animals.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> The Technocracy essentially became the very thing the Order of Reason was started to oppose (the elitism of the mages against the common man) while the younger generations of the Traditions have started to come around to the Craftsmasons line of reasoning... that the common man can be elevated by sharing the wonder of magick with them.<br /> <br /> History is cyclical for a reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T09:36:16-07:00","id":1386991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386975#post1386975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does, however, point out one of the potential differences between what the Technocracy does and what everyone else does: the Technocracy eventually gets its innovations into the hands of ordinary citizens. That is, after sufficient \u201cterranorming\u201d (if I'm understanding the term right), things that started out as Inventions that only Enlightened Scientists could use can eventually end up as common, everyday fixtures in everyone's household. While theoretically the Traditions <i>could</i> replicate this feat, in practice they don't: if you want to benefit from faith healing, you have to rely on the generosity of a faith healer.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, in the paradigm of faith healing, you could literally pray the disease away.<br /> <br /> It's the technocracy that instaured the system of &quot;giving them new tech slowly&quot;, it is not the universal way things works. That's why the traditions are not trying to give their spells to the sleepers, but make them believe in magic overall.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To the extent that the Traditions care about the common man, it's largely in reaction to the Technocracy's very real inroads in that regard. But absent that reaction, Tradition goals tend to focus more on empowering the mage, with the Sleepers benefitting from a sort of \u201ctrickle down effect\u201d: if mages are empowered, then the communities that they favor will benefit from that: if the master does well, so will his servants. In contrast, the Technocracy tends to try to empower the Masses directly (or at least they did, until they went off the rails).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That apply to the order of hermes and the akashic brotherhood. And that's pretty much it.<br /> The chorus is all about the common man, his well being and his connection to the One, the ecstatics want everyone to feel the world as much as they do, the dreamspeakers and verbena roles was always to act as the middle man between supernatural forces and their communities, the Euthanatos are pretty much only about the lives of sleepers, and the etherites and virtuals are concerned about upgradding the lives of everyone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T10:01:36-07:00","id":1387002,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the Traditions folow some sort of Prime Directive of non-interference? In another closely related game, it is written into the Oath of Hermes (&quot;I will not endanger the Order through my actions. Nor will I interfere with the affaires of mundanes andf thereby bring ruin on my sodales. I will not deal with devils, lest I imperil my soul, and the souls of my sodalis as well. I will not molest the faeries, lest their vengence catch my sodalis also&quot;)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386990#post1386990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also worth noting in regards to the science vs. magic split is that, before they founded the Order of Reason, the Craftsmasons were members of the Order of Hermes\u2019 House ex Miscellanea (one of the reasons Clan Tremere always has influence over various Mason organizations in my Vampire-exclusive games... ever wonder why they do so many blood drives?)..</div> </div> </div> </div>Fascinating. Where can I track down that tidbit? I have a fond curiosity for Freemasonry. This is interesting. In another related game, in a book that I helped write, *after* the assault on Mistridge, the Craftmasons equivalent (the Rusticani) were absorbed into Ex-Miscellanea. Before that they were considered Hedge Wizards.<br /> But back to mage, I sorta want to reintroduce Craftmasons into the modern setting. On which side? Who knows. But I imagine that a typical Lodge is 99% normal mundanes. One member of each lodge is secretly a wizard of some sort.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T10:16:03-07:00","id":1387006,"title":"","content":"With all due respect, no. Every last one of these groups, even when they benefit the common man, do so through the agency of the mage. The shaman is the intermediary; without him, the people are at the mercy of the spirits. The Verbena place the blessings and curses on people; the power remains invested in them. Not just anyone's prayers suffice where the Celestial Chorus is concerned: it needs to be the prayers of the Holy Man or the clergy. The Ecstatic <i>does</i> want everyone to experience the same things they do; and to that end, they seek ways to encourage people to Awaken. But until a Sleeper Awakens, the Cult of Ecstasy doesn't do much for them. And so on. Again, the Traditions are primarily there for the benefit of the Awakened; the Sleepers only benefit to the extent that the Awakened decide to help them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-05-2021, 06:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T10:34:38-07:00","id":1387011,"title":"","content":"@dataweaver: That seems a bit off. From my understanding, with regards to the chorus, for example: if it had to be the holy man or the clergy all the time, they would never encourage the layperson to pray... Instead they seem to work miracles to help people and show people that people's faith will cause miracles or cause their God to cause miracles... And if one person can't do this alone, the proper thing to do is to get more people to pray. Many voices one song. And by mage Ascension logic, if the consensus was more attuned to their idea, all you'd need to achieve good things is to pray faithfully a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T11:12:55-07:00","id":1387019,"title":"","content":"Lay people can assist a holy man with their prayers. But they can't do it themselves. Not until they Awaken. And that's the main thrust of the Traditions with respect to Sleepers: \u201cwe'll help you by helping you Awaken.\u201d<br /> <br /> <i>Could</i> they achieve a future where even Sleepers could get tangible benefits from prayer, without a holy man being involved? Possibly. There would be challenges in doing so; but if the Technocracy can do it, it's at least possible that the Traditions might be able to as well. However, it tends to be a moot point in that the Traditions tend not to be interested in trying to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-09-2020, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T11:34:39-07:00","id":1387024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387019#post1387019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lay people can assist a holy man with their prayers. But they can't do it themselves. Not until they Awaken. And that's the main thrust of the Traditions with respect to Sleepers: \u201cwe'll help you by helping you Awaken.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's only true with a consensus that reject the power of prayer. Same as using a computer in the 18th century. But if the Consensus acknowledge the power of prayer, everyone will be able to pray away issues.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's literally the premise of the Ascension war.<br /> <br /> And it match Dark ages systems, in which people could access &quot;incantations&quot; true faith was more common and alchemy was a capacity. In fact, the chorus simply try to bring that back, but with the twist that anyone can talk to the one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A good exemple of what may happen is one of the alternate world scenario in either the book of mirrors or the book of secrets, I don't remember exactly which one, in which the traditions take over the consensus, and every sleeper end up gaining the equivalent of a 1 or 2 level magical effect of power because they acknowledge that &quot;everyone has magic&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","user":"Nyremne","date":". 05-09-2020, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T12:05:25-07:00","id":1387035,"title":"","content":"Dataweaver is right that these groups operate under the agency of mages, and primarily for the benefit of mages. But that's true of the Technocracy too. The Union might give Sleepers more toys, and more of an illusion of agency, but the Union does its best to ensure Sleepers never have toys that are a threat to Technocratic control, just enough to keep them happier under Union thumb than other options.<br /> <br /> However, that doesn't mean non-Technocracy primary Reality Zones have no potential benefits for Sleepers in terms of access to things. The editions are just kind of inconsistent about how that's supposed to work out. A Hermetic dominated reality would be a massive boon for the spread of Sorcerers, as anyone that studies hard enough could learn some level of linear magic according to the Hermetics. And, of course, such Reality Zones are a huge benefit to sapient non-humans... which is an entirely different wrinkle in any such calculations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T12:38:58-07:00","id":1387046,"title":"","content":"Guess why bows went out of style? Because to properly teach an archer, you had to \u201cstart with his grandfather\u201d. Archery required a lot of physical conditioning and training. When black powder weapons came on the scene, they didn't really have any more range, lethality, or rate of fire than longbows had. What they <i>did</i> have was that anyone could use them with minimal training. <br /> <br /> Even in the mystical paradigms where prayers work for Sleepers, it isn't that <i>just any</i> prayer will work for anyone; that remains the purview of the Awakened. For a Sleeper to be able to work miracles without the intervention of one of the Awakened, the Sleeper needs to be initiated into a religious order that will teach them how to properly pray (in game terms, the Sleeper needs to jump through the hoops required to become a Sorcerer, and then learn appropriate Paths). This isn't as hard to do as it is to get someone to Awaken; but it's not trivial either. <br /> <br /> The main reason why the Technocracy has been so successful has been a one-two punch of Devices and Terranorming. The first part is that the Technocracy can mass-produce Devices, whereas every Talisman that a mage makes is an intensely personal affair (as reflected in the requirement to invest <i>dots</i> of Willpower into the Talisman, plus personal Quintessence into the crafting process). This is true even of the Sons of Ether and Virtual Adepts. (Personal aside: I suspect that the secret to this mass-production lies in Primal Utility, making it something of a Syndicate trade secret.) The second part is that if the Device produces an Adjustment (i.e., a Coincidental Effect), it can be used by anyone with minimal training, as opposed to Devices that generate Vulgar Effects which can only be used by Extraordinary Citizens or Enlightened Sciences. By engaging in Terranorming, the Technocracy can greatly increase the selection of Devices that can be used by anyone. <br /> <br /> The Traditions can do the Terranorming thing, too; though it's possible that the Technocracy can take it a step further than the Traditions can here too, and with sufficiently advanced Terranorming techniques moved some Devices from Coincidental to downright <i>mundane</i>, where they're not even Wonders anymore (meaning that Sleepers can <i>make</i> them as well as use them) \u2014 though that's just speculation on my part. But as I said before, the Traditions can't mass-produce Talismans. <br /> <br /> And they can't mass-produce sorcerers, either. If there's a way to do that, the secret to doing so is more likely to be found in the Technocracy's paradigm than the Traditions': the Technocrats can mass-produce Principiae, too; the Traditions cannot mass-produce Grimoires. <br /> <br /> And while I've been saying a lot about what the Traditions <i>can't</i> do, a case could be made that they can't because they haven't bothered to try: mass-production of Wonders isn't something that interests the Traditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T12:44:19-07:00","id":1387047,"title":"","content":"It's a fundamental fact that the Traditions are built around the idea of Mass Ascension. They are not, never, and never will be about hoarding magic since the establishment of the Nine. The Technocracy is also built around this idea. Neither party actually has any disagreement that everyone in the world should Awaken, theoretically. There was the EVIL Progenitor plan in the original 1st Edition books to get rid of avatars so the Sleepers could be controlled but that was an example of EVIL [mind you, in RL, we know there's actually plots by the Far Right to destroy education in America and other countries because they believe it will help the Masses be easier to control].<br /> <br /> Indeed, that was actually a big thing about Revised initially that was so controversial. The Ascension War ended because the developers pointed out that the Union and Traditions actually had very little reason to actually hate one another [except the literally thousands of dead killed in the war so far]. At the time, and I was a Mage player then, it was, &quot;There's homelessness in the streets! Why are you fighting over Saturn!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387046#post1387046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guess why bows went out of style? Because to properly teach an archer, you had to \u201cstart with his grandfather\u201d. Archery required a lot of physical conditioning and training. When black powder weapons came on the scene, they didn't really have any more range, lethality, or rate of fire than longbows had. What they <i>did</i> have was that anyone could use them with minimal training.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is essentially saying the Union is right, which is taking a position the games have never done. Especially since the two options presented are:<br /> <br /> 1. The Union has won and the world they've created is the World of Darkness.<br /> 2. The Union has lost and humanity is going to exterminate itself.<br /> <br /> SCIENCE, FUCK YEAH is not an option. Especially when the premise is science if you suppress facts [magic is real], murder your dissidents, and round people up into MECHA camps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-09-2020, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T13:20:10-07:00","id":1387057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386932#post1386932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That gets into crypto-history but if there's a Mythic Age of the World of Darkness wouldn't they have actually created a China that had things like dragons, alchemical immortality, and armies of clay warriors? Plus, wouldn't prayer actually have healed people in the Middle Ages? Because once we start down this rabbit hole, we start getting the fact that the history of magick in the WOD isn't the history of our world.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're still not getting it. Of course there were miracles where prayer healed people in the Middle Ages. As you would say, &quot;you're not accepting the premise of the game&quot;! Except I'm pretty sure you do allow members of the Celestial Chorus to heal people through their prayers in your game.<br /> <br /> It's just that prayer didn't lead to the end of disease. It was still present everywhere. So your point that the Technocracy is bad because it is somehow holding back some kind of universal panacea, but the Traditions wouldn't still fails. That the Celestial Chorus could heal individual members through prayer didn't matter when the Black Death arrived (and all the other diseases that made sure one-third of all children in the pre-modern world died before the age of five). So we're back to the fact that they didn't help babies.<br /> <br /> One of the tensions in the game is that despite the fact that PCs and NPCs in Mage can do all these wonderful things, that essentially nothing that can be noticed by ordinary people seems to have changed from our own world. That isn't unique to the World of Darkness. It's found in most urban fantasy settings and mainstream superhero universes. It's just a part of certain genres. Because if you did allow major departures in the game world, you don't have the World of Darkness or a &quot;world outside your door&quot;, but some kind of obvious fantasy setting. Any historical deviations as a result of mages, vampires, and the like would have to be unnoticed or of trivial importance. Instead it becomes a trick of trying to figure out how real world history happened in the game because of all these supernatural forces out there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386932#post1386932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then we also question, &quot;Wait, the Technocracy didn't exist until the 14th century, doesn't that mean the Order of Hermes created running water and indoor plumbing in Rome?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because the Order of Hermes wasn't concerned about running water or indoor plumbing. That's still part of the early tradition of the Technocratic Union despite being done back then because only the forerunners of the technocracy were really interested in practical things like engineering. The Hermetic Order was still interested in esoteric wisdom, summoning up spirits, alchemy, and the like. <br /> <br /> It's just that the paradigm of the Classical World still allowed for the Hermetics and people like Archimedes to exist side by side. There was no struggle back then to impose one Paradigm over the other en masse.<br /> <br /> The only time I would say groups like the Hermetics, Cult of Isis, and the like would be involved in more &quot;scientific&quot; projects would be ones where we can interpret with all sorts of astrological, numerological, or other mystical importance like Stonehenge or the Pyramids. But anything mundane (though awesome) like Roman aqueducts, sewers, and such - nope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T13:21:56-07:00","id":1387059,"title":"","content":"Cool argument, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> but I don't think it fits my mage very well. Thanks for sharing! I think that's too nice of a Technocracy and Order of Reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T14:09:02-07:00","id":1387077,"title":"","content":"Sure thing. I enjoyed your debate too. <br /> <br /> But I don't think the issue is really between your version of the Technocracy and mine. I'm perfectly fine that the Technocracy has evolved into a tyrannical, authoritarian organization based on control doing all the evil sorts of things you mentioned in your first post. (And the fact that they cause great harm doesn't mean they can't do good at the same time - Mussolini made the trains run on time, and the Nazis instituted the world's first environmental laws, animal protection acts, restrictions on tobacco because of health issues, and improved welfare. But that didn't change that they were criminal tyrants.)<br /> <br /> I think the difference is that your <i>Traditions</i> are too nice. It's that you are insisting the Traditions are this group of goody White Hats who only want the best interests on mankind as opposed to flawed people who are sometimes prone to abusing their own powers, or concentrating on their own solipsistic obsessions. To me, the Traditions are much more grey despite being spiritually enlightened to a degree and many coming from altruistic backgrounds. There are good members and bad members, and even the good members sometimes end up doing bad things. And there are simply limits to what they can achieve because of Paradox or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T15:18:52-07:00","id":1387091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387047#post1387047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a fundamental fact that the Traditions are built around the idea of Mass Ascension. They are not, never, and never will be about hoarding magic since the establishment of the Nine. The Technocracy is also built around this idea. Neither party actually has any disagreement that everyone in the world should Awaken, theoretically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. First, I never said that the Traditions are about hoarding magick: anyone who can Awaken is welcomed with open arms, and the Traditions encourage Awakenings to the best of their ability. It's just that the primary value they attach to Sleepers lies with their potential to Awaken. <br /> <br /> Second, the Traditions may express an interest <i>in theory</i> of everyone Awakening; but most acknowledge that that's an unattainable ideal; certainly not something that's going to be achieved in the foreseeable future. And not <i>just</i> because of existing conditions in the ground; unless and until they find a reliable way to Awaken people, there's no way to attain Mass Ascension. <br /> <br /> As far as the Technocracy goes, I'm not sure that they <i>are</i> interested in Mass Ascension. Sure, they've got their Utopian visions of the future; but by and large, every last one of them would put some sort of restriction on who can Awaken. Not because they don't want to empower people; they arguably do, even now. But from their perspective, Awakening everyone would be the height of irresponsibility. So you really want to give that kind of power to madmen and monsters who just want to see the world burn? Because Marauders and Nephandi are a thing, even if you're willing to accept that the Traditions' behavior is tolerable (which, outside of the Syndicate and the Void Engineers, isn't a popular view). <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Traditions are like the gun nuts who want everyone to be able to own a firearm, no matter what.<br /> <br /> Put another way, Mass Ascension may not be the great good that the Traditions make it out to be. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387047#post1387047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was the EVIL Progenitor plan in the original 1st Edition books to get rid of avatars so the Sleepers could be controlled but that was an example of EVIL [mind you, in RL, we know there's actually plots by the Far Right to destroy education in America and other countries because they believe it will help the Masses be easier to control].</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, that would be plots by the Far Left to pervert education in America and other countries because they believe it will help the Masses be easier to control. See my suggestion to review the Politics in M20 thread: the Technocracy isn't Right Wing, and the Traditions aren't liberal champions; nor is the opposite true. Setting aside whether or not the stereotypes you ascribe to the IRL political wings are overly simplistic and/or just plain wrong, the in-game groups bear at best a passing resemblance to them. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387047#post1387047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is essentially saying the Union is right, which is taking a position the games have never done.</div> </div> </div> </div> No; it's saying that the Technocracy may have a valid point or two, which is something that the game <i>has</i> done. But I'll note that you didn't actually address my argument; you just said \u201cit makes the Technocracy look good, so it must be wrong\u201d without any mention of what's wrong with it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387047#post1387047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially since the two options presented are:<br /> <br /> 1. The Union has won and the world they've created is the World of Darkness.<br /> 2. The Union has lost and humanity is going to exterminate itself.<br /> <br /> SCIENCE, FUCK YEAH is not an option. Especially when the premise is science if you suppress facts [magic is real], murder your dissidents, and round people up into MECHA camps.</div> </div> </div> </div> Except that that doesn't change the fact that the Technocracy (or rather, the Order or Reason) <i>was</i> founded on \u201cSCIENCE! FUCK YEAH!\u201d See <b>Sorcerers Crusade</b> which, like M20 with the Technocracy, presented the Daedalians in a flawed but positive light and as a playable faction, just like it did with the Traditions. <br /> <br /> And there's a third option: the Technocracy has won some, and lost some; but the fight continues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-29-2021, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T15:38:34-07:00","id":1387098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387091#post1387091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that that doesn't change the fact that the Technocracy (or rather, the Order or Reason) <i>was</i> founded on \u201cSCIENCE! FUCK YEAH!\u201d See <b>Sorcerers Crusade</b> which, like M20 with the Technocracy, presented the Daedalians in a flawed but positive light and as a playable faction, just like it did with the Traditions.<br /> <br /> And there's a third option: the Technocracy has won some, and lost some; but the fight continues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Random aside, it's always been weird to me that the Order of Reason is treated as the BAD one and the Technocracy as a perversion of its ideas. The Order of Reason seems like it would be the Technocracy at its worst with colonialism, slavery, and genocide being common things.<br /> <br /> While the Technocracy would be a group that is more globalist and arguably reformed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T15:40:16-07:00","id":1387099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387019#post1387019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, it tends to be a moot point in that the Traditions tend not to be interested in trying to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think, not interested is quite right either. More like collectively incapable despite the great desire of a fraction of their membership. Basically, the problem isn't that they don't want to do great things to help the world, it's that they had terrible leadership that was more self absorbed than anything else and even without that leadership can't agree on an overall program for the Tradition as a whole and concentrate their power on a unified goal. So instead, each tradition does its own thing, with some having each subgroup doing it's own thing in ways that can easily be shut down by a Unified force, like the Technocracy. The way I read them, the vast majority of non hermetic mages are idealists who don't really get the bigger picture, but the hermetic mages were mostly the ones calling the shots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T15:45:20-07:00","id":1387101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387099#post1387099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think, not interested is quite right either. More like collectively incapable despite the great desire of a fraction of their membership. Basically, the problem isn't that they don't want to do great things to help the world, it's that they had terrible leadership that was more self absorbed than anything else and even without that leadership can't agree on an overall program for the Tradition as a whole and concentrate their power on a unified goal. So instead, each tradition does its own thing, with some having each subgroup doing it's own thing in ways that can easily be shut down by a Unified force, like the Technocracy. The way I read them, the vast majority of non hermetic mages are idealists who don't really get the bigger picture, but the hermetic mages were mostly the ones calling the shots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's my 1st Edition feeling going but I imagine part of it is also the fact that any mage who has any sort of public profile will be hunted down and murdered. I always imagined something similar to NOWHERE MAN or THE MATRIX in that mages are people who live in hiding.<br /> <br /> The Union doesn't tolerate them to live prior to M:TA:R<br /> <br /> They can and will kill and replace you if you are discovered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" ta