amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T16:01:19-07:00","id":1387111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387105#post1387105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The books seem to take an Out of Character view it was an idealistic and heroic group of people trying to save the Masses while the Union is corrupt and about accumulating power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just took it that to mean that the Order followed great ideals but ended up doing terrible things in their hubris and that the book kinda looks at them with a standard closer to the thinking of a romanticized version oft that age, which is what the book is about... While we get a more realistic modern view of the Union in it's revised version book. But I get what you are saying now that I compare them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T16:05:17-07:00","id":1387113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387109#post1387109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought Revised outright ended the Ascension War.</div> </div> </div> </div>It did, but the Union simply deprioritized mage hunts. They still killed or captured any mages that got in their way or made good targets of opportunity and we're more open to some level of unofficial tolerance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T16:16:07-07:00","id":1387116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387099#post1387099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think, not interested is quite right either. More like collectively incapable despite the great desire of a fraction of their membership. Basically, the problem isn't that they don't want to do great things to help the world, it's that they had terrible leadership that was more self absorbed than anything else and even without that leadership can't agree on an overall program for the Tradition as a whole and concentrate their power on a unified goal. So instead, each tradition does its own thing, with some having each subgroup doing it's own thing in ways that can easily be shut down by a Unified force, like the Technocracy. The way I read them, the vast majority of non hermetic mages are idealists who don't really get the bigger picture, but the hermetic mages were mostly the ones calling the shots.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have to disagree with this, too. First, the Order of Hermes is not the Secret Masters of the Traditions (or even the Not So Secret Masters). There's no way the other eight Traditions would stand for the Order of Hermes dictating to them. <br /> <br /> But second, the idea that the typical Traditionist is an altruist who wants to make the world a better place is mainly Tradition propaganda. There <i>are</i> Traditionists like that (if you want, your group's protagonists can be among them); but by design, they're the exception. (I remember a few times on these boards \u2014 or rather, on the predecessors to these forums \u2014 where Mage developers expressly commented that the Traditions really aren't that much better than the Technocracy, with the intent being that the player characters can be the exceptions trying to reform the Traditions. Not unlike their intentions for Technocracy-centered material. <br /> <br /> And to the extent that they <i>are</i> altruistic, it tends to take the form of \u201cpeople will be better off if they Awaken\u201d \u2014 thus the Traditions' so far unsuccessful search for a way to reliably trigger Awakenings. Since they <i>haven't</i> achieved such a technique, the question of whether or not it would be a good thing is moot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T18:31:04-07:00","id":1387142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387116#post1387116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll have to disagree with this, too. First, the Order of Hermes is not the Secret Masters of the Traditions (or even the Not So Secret Masters). There's no way the other eight Traditions would stand for the Order of Hermes dictating to them. <br /> <br /> But second, the idea that the typical Traditionist is an altruist who wants to make the world a better place is mainly Tradition propaganda. There <i>are</i> Traditionists like that (if you want, your group's protagonists can be among them); but by design, they're the exception. (I remember a few times on these boards \u2014 or rather, on the predecessors to these forums \u2014 where Mage developers expressly commented that the Traditions really aren't that much better than the Technocracy, with the intent being that the player characters can be the exceptions trying to reform the Traditions. Not unlike their intentions for Technocracy-centered material. <br /> <br /> And to the extent that they <i>are</i> altruistic, it tends to take the form of \u201cpeople will be better off if they Awaken\u201d \u2014 thus the Traditions' so far unsuccessful search for a way to reliably trigger Awakenings. Since they <i>haven't</i> achieved such a technique, the question of whether or not it would be a good thing is moot.</div> </div> </div> </div>With regards to leadership the Order of Hermes, maybe calling the shots is a bit overboard but &quot; the order of Hermes is, often fairly, accused of holding power over the affairs of the Traditions out of keeping with it's size. In many cases, of inter-tradition politics, there are whole systems of governance over which the order wields a virtual monopoly.&quot; Is something said out of character in the Order of Hermes book.<br /> <br /> Just to be clear though, I said the vast majority of non Hermetics are idealists, not altruists <br /> <br /> To be more specific, the akashic think people will probably eventually walk and find their path to the way. The euthanatos kill with the best of intentions, the choristers have all manner of unrealistic idealism in their heads about everyone uniting, the etherites think science can solve things outside the scope of science, the VA think that their war against the establishment is righteous and going somewhere, the ecstatics don't realize how addictive their tools are, etc. Mostly, the Hermetics just want to gain magical power, in my opinion. Most of the other traditions have some semblance of the good of the people imbedded in their philosophies, the same way the tech does. The difference is the tech has a coherent plan and they don't, is what I was saying.<br /> <br /> As for self absorbed leaders, most of the guys in the book about Horizon were who I was calling self absorbed, with a few exceptions. Not just the order of Hermes guy. So bad leadership all around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T18:39:32-07:00","id":1387146,"title":"","content":"I think the Order of Hermes is kind of like the Ventrue for the Traditions in that it's not so much they control the Camarilla as they're one of the few groups actually invested in it at all as an organization. They want to have the meetings, minutes, diplomatic conferences, and 5 year plans.<br /> <br /> The others are like, &quot;Sure man, whatever.&quot;<br /> <br /> The others all have their own internal organizations and would be more interested in NATO versus an actual single group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T19:21:41-07:00","id":1387155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387101#post1387101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it's my 1st Edition feeling going</div> </div> </div> </div>...yeah in general I wouldn't put too much stock in the 1e depictions of the factions, since those had the Traditions being Paragon Good Guys and Technocracy as Objectively Evil guys. Something that 2e-M20 walked back from.<br /> <br /> Unless, of course, you prefer them to be that way at your table...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T19:33:22-07:00","id":1387156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387155#post1387155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...yeah in general I wouldn't put too much stock in the 1e depictions of the factions, since those had the Traditions being Paragon Good Guys and Technocracy as Objectively Evil guys. Something that 2e-M20 walked back from.<br /> <br /> Unless, of course, you prefer them to be that way at your table...</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, generally I prefer to play Technocracy games but it's with the caveat that I tend to play my Technocracy games like I play my Vampire: The Masquerade games. I've run about six Technocrat campaigns and about 2 Tradition ones in my entire history of gaming since the Nineties.<br /> <br /> <b>How do I run the Technocracy?</b><br /> <br /> I draw from the old TV show La Femme Nikita and emphasize the paranoia and fear of being a Technocrat. Your bosses can and will order you &quot;cancelled&quot; at any given moment and you have no option of resigning or disobeying orders. Brainwashing happens but most Technocrats have a low level of it so they can have very low morale. They buy deeply into the &quot;hard man, making hard choices&quot; ideology with the view that if you're not willing to kill a innocent man to save 100 (or who your superiors say will do it) you're not playing ball. You do, however, get face to face with lots of much-worse people in the world. Corruption is very casual with cloned sex slaves, embezzlement, mortal prejudices, and use of Union power to increase your own personal power. In-fighting is constant between Conventions and individual constructs.<br /> <br /> <b>How do I run the Traditions?</b><br /> <br /> I've never run a Chantry game. Both my campaigns have been street level with the premise that the Technocracy is always watching you and if you're found out, you will be killed. Your family will also probably be kidnapped, brainwashed, or cloned and replaced if you don't run from them as well as cut all ties. You have to live off the grid and maintaining a mortal identity is incredibly difficult. Expect your mortal identity to have been suddenly wanted in six states for felony murder, pedophilia, or other crimes you didn't commit. The Traditions when they showed up are effectively lunatics who live in Narnia rather than try to live in the real world. They're often completely at odds with &quot;normal&quot; people and aren't especially concerned with their lives.<br /> <br /> I view these as my own canon versus a proper version of either. Effectively, I ran Disparate games instead of Tradition ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-10-2020, 01:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T22:33:10-07:00","id":1387186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387156#post1387156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I admit, generally I prefer to play Technocracy games but it's with the caveat that I tend to play my Technocracy games like I play my Vampire: The Masquerade games. I've run about six Technocrat campaigns and about 2 Tradition ones in my entire history of gaming since the Nineties.<br /> <br /> <b>How do I run the Technocracy?</b><br /> <br /> I draw from the old TV show La Femme Nikita and emphasize the paranoia and fear of being a Technocrat. Your bosses can and will order you &amp;quot;cancelled&amp;quot; at any given moment and you have no option of resigning or disobeying orders. Brainwashing happens but most Technocrats have a low level of it so they can have very low morale. They buy deeply into the &amp;quot;hard man, making hard choices&amp;quot; ideology with the view that if you're not willing to kill a innocent man to save 100 (or who your superiors say will do it) you're not playing ball. You do, however, get face to face with lots of much-worse people in the world. Corruption is very casual with cloned sex slaves, embezzlement, mortal prejudices, and use of power to increase your own personal power. In-fighting is constant between Conventions and individual constructs.<br /> <br /> <b>How do I run the Traditions?</b><br /> <br /> I've never run a Chantry game. Both my campaigns have been street level with the premise that the Technocracy is always watching you and if you're found out, you will be killed. Your family will also probably be kidnapped, brainwashed, or cloned and replaced if you don't run from them as well as cut all ties. You have to live off the grid and maintaining a mortal identity is incredibly difficult. Expect your mortal identity to have been suddenly wanted in six states for felony murder, pedophilia, or other crimes you didn't commit. The Traditions when they showed up are effectively lunatics who live in Narnia rather than try to live in the real world. They're often completely at odds with &amp;quot;normal&amp;quot; people and aren't especially concerned with their lives.<br /> <br /> I view these as my own canon versus a proper version of either. Effectively, I ran Disparate games instead of Tradition ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have 1st Ed Technocrat operatives with late 2nd Edition characitures of Horizon Realm OoH playing the part of Traditions.<br /> <br /> This entire topic is making a lot more...sense isn't the right word...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T22:42:35-07:00","id":1387188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387186#post1387186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have 1st Ed Technocrat operatives with late 2nd Edition caricatures of Horizon Realm OoH playing the part of Traditions.<br /> <br /> This entire topic is making a lot more...sense isn't the right word...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's like being in the Camarilla when you're a Technocrat. The organization is a bulwark against even worse forces out there but has succumbed to its own vices and lust for power. However, if you kill the bad guys in the organization above you, you can take it over and reform it. Or maybe you just want to survive.<br /> <br /> As for the Traditions, why bother living on Earth when you can be a god of your own little pocket dimension? Mage Separatism is better than living among the ignorant masses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-10-2020, 01:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T23:26:22-07:00","id":1387196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387188#post1387188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Traditions, why bother living on Earth when you can be a god of your own little pocket dimension? Mage Separatism is better than living among the ignorant masses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well. Peacing out to your own Horizon Realm is hardly easy, especially since starting mage PCs don't have the Spheres to make one themselves. And the climb to get there is a long one, unless if the ST is REALLY liberal with the EXP, or house ruled the EXP-rate down...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T03:02:33-07:00","id":1387215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marko Markoko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387002#post1387002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps the Traditions folow some sort of Prime Directive of non-interference? In another closely related game, it is written into the Oath of Hermes (&quot;I will not endanger the Order through my actions. Nor will I interfere with the affaires of mundanes andf thereby bring ruin on my sodales. I will not deal with devils, lest I imperil my soul, and the souls of my sodalis as well. I will not molest the faeries, lest their vengence catch my sodalis also&quot;)<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>They don't, The Chorus is out there helping people, the etherites are constantly trying to break throught the scientific community, the guide to the tradition have a few exemples of mages invoquing spirits to talk to the radio to inspire people....<br /> <br /> In the end, the only answer to that conundrum is &quot;the technocracy is stopping them&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T03:12:48-07:00","id":1387216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387215#post1387215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They don't, The Chorus is out there helping people, the etherites are constantly trying to break throught the scientific community, the guide to the tradition have a few exemples of mages invoquing spirits to talk to the radio to inspire people....<br /> <br /> In the end, the only answer to that conundrum is &quot;the technocracy is stopping them&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, also Paradox.<br /> <br /> The Taftani are kind of a ticking time bomb of self-inflicted death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T03:14:02-07:00","id":1387217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387091#post1387091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Y<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Traditions are like the gun nuts who want everyone to be able to own a firearm, no matter what.<br /> <br /> Put another way, Mass Ascension may not be the great good that the Traditions make it out to be.<br /> <br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's not a fair comparison. Owning a firearm and being enlightened to the nature of reality with the ability to shape it are not equivalent.<br /> <br /> Mass Ascension means notably that the barrier sleeper/awakened will no longuer exist. It is literally a world of infinite possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T03:19:32-07:00","id":1387218,"title":"","content":"The Technocracy Reloaded interviews have been going on about the very strange idea that they've been giving humanity TOO MUCH knowledge about science and technology, so the Sleepers are the enemy with their ignorance.<br /> <br /> Which is....I am really surprised by that turn of events.<br /> <br /> But it's an interesting take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T03:57:58-07:00","id":1387238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387218#post1387218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Technocracy Reloaded interviews have been going on about the very strange idea that they've been giving humanity TOO MUCH knowledge about science and technology, so the Sleepers are the enemy with their ignorance.<br /> <br /> Which is....I am really surprised by that turn of events.<br /> <br /> But it's an interesting take.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That sound contradictory, how did they frame that concept?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T04:04:33-07:00","id":1387240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387238#post1387238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sound contradictory, how did they frame that concept?</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently, the RL politics of anti-vaxxers, internet trolls, authoritarian dictatorships, fake news, and so on are all blamed by the Technocracy on the Sleepers misusing their gifts. This is apparenty a theme and why they're seeking out Tradition help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T06:37:21-07:00","id":1387259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387217#post1387217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not a fair comparison. Owning a firearm and being enlightened to the nature of reality with the ability to shape it are not equivalent.</div> </div> </div> </div> You're right; that's not a fair comparison. Being able to shape reality is <i>far</i> more dangerous than being able to fire a gun. The former can be abused in ways limited only by the imagination; the latter is equivalent to a single mid-level Forces rote, possibly with a touch of Correspondence for accuracy. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387217#post1387217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mass Ascension means notably that the barrier sleeper/awakened will no longuer exist. It is literally a world of infinite possibilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026where every demented monster and madman has infinite possibilities with which to torment others. Just look at the <b>Book of the Fallen</b>, and picture what happens when <i>everyone</i> with that mindset Awakens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T06:45:33-07:00","id":1387262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387240#post1387240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently, the RL politics of anti-vaxxers, internet trolls, authoritarian dictatorships, fake news, and so on are all blamed by the Technocracy on the Sleepers misusing their gifts. This is apparenty a theme and why they're seeking out Tradition help.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear, \u201cmass stupidity by Sleepers abusing our gifts\u201d is mentioned in the introduction, as part of \u201cwe've been derelict in our duties by giving the Masses more than they were ready to handle\u201d. The \u201cAscension Truce\u201d (where the Technocracy reaches out to the Traditions to try to come up with a solution to this) is a Unit 8 \u201cFuture Fate\u201d entry: one possibility for what comes next, which may or may not happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T08:18:26-07:00","id":1387500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387099#post1387099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think, not interested is quite right either. More like collectively incapable despite the great desire of a fraction of their membership. Basically, the problem isn't that they don't want to do great things to help the world, it's that they had terrible leadership that was more self absorbed than anything else and even without that leadership can't agree on an overall program for the Tradition as a whole and concentrate their power on a unified goal. So instead, each tradition does its own thing, with some having each subgroup doing it's own thing in ways that can easily be shut down by a Unified force, like the Technocracy. The way I read them, the vast majority of non hermetic mages are idealists who don't really get the bigger picture, but the hermetic mages were mostly the ones calling the shots.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it's my 1st Edition feeling going but I imagine part of it is also the fact that any mage who has any sort of public profile will be hunted down and murdered. I always imagined something similar to NOWHERE MAN or THE MATRIX in that mages are people who live in hiding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bad leadership and opression surely have a role, but let's not neglect what's just the Paradigm expressing itself.<br /> <br /> For instance: Much has been said about the chorus good will for normal people. But let's think a little about how their magick actually works:. The chorus posits that prayer can cure disease, yes...<i>but it's enough to just go with the motions?</i>, I think the Chorus it's prety clear about the prayers being backed by <b>faith</b><br /> <br /> In the Bible you have people doing miracles...but it's this <b>really </b>a characteristic of the <i>common man</i>? I'm always amazed people believes religion it's *that* nice: I seem to remember that even an apostle failed to walk over water once, because he lacked enough faith. I seem to remember that faith was, indeed, able to move mountains - but for a man that had plucked his own eyes because they had dared to tempt him to sin...are these common people?<i> I find odd to think that the mage faction that's based on these stories would believe that</i> <i>everyone's faith it's equal</i>.<br /> <br /> A farmer could have the same faith, and thus the same or even more power granted by God, as any ordained priests/preachers/whatever. Potentially. But that's far from certain and usually not expected by people that follows religious Paradigms.<br /> That's why you bother to go the the holly man to do the lay on hands instead of just staying in your home and doing a quick pray. Religion isn't: &quot;I pray and everything I want<i> just happens</i>&quot;, it's &quot;I pray because it's the correct thing to do, and then God will say what happens&quot; - with a lot of &quot;yes, there are people that are more spiritual than me - hence why I go to the preacher when I have a problem instead of just praying at home&quot;<br /> <br /> From the POV of mystical paradigms, power comes from the self - but people aren't all made equal. Hence the elitism of the Traditions. The Technocratic revolution was not requiring from people actual faith in the scientific method. For Tech, it IS enough to go with the motions (or at least it should be)<br /> <br /> If the Chorus were to win the AW, prayer should be more effective than it's now, but not necesarilly AS effective. In the DA: Mage setting they had the dominant Paradigm over Europe, and prayers certainly *did stuff*, yet sickness and suffering were very much a thing. Would it have been different if they had the World instead? . Maybe, but I think there's enough evidence to seed plausible deniability to the idea that the Chorus can create a world where everyone can cure with a clap of their hands <i>so easily</i><br /> <br /> ...not the least because that's not how actual religion works: Not everyone it's supposed to cure with just an utterance, not a single religious belief I know suggest such a fantasyland world w/o sickness and suffering before the End of Days: Are we going to say that Christianity admiting not everyone has, nor will have, Faith before Apocalipse it's the Techncoracy's doing too?. Are we going to give Choristers such a much more hopeful worldview than any actual RL religion, as to have them sincerely believe otherwise?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Random aside, it's always been weird to me that the Order of Reason is treated as the BAD one and the Technocracy as a perversion of its ideas. The Order of Reason seems like it would be the Technocracy at its worst with colonialism, slavery, and genocide being common things.<br /> <br /> While the Technocracy would be a group that is more globalist and arguably reformed. </div> </div> </div>Technocracy was founded in the Victorian era, I think colonization and genoside weren't over yet. India comes to mind. And it can be argued that the Technocracy had more to do with the colonial *exploits* of English imperialism than they had with the colonization of america (Since the Queen actually knew of the Technocracy and was onboard with them).<br /> <br /> Afterwards they were behind the 1\u00b0 WW technological advancements in killing. Latter they had no problem in helping the Nazi develop, until they discovered that there were Nephandi behind it (near the end of WW2), one of the reasons of VA defection was that the Technocracy was unconcerned with the mortal Nazi's doings (and unlike the Traditions, they can't claim this wasn't policy but the work of rogue individuals - the Technocracy it's capable of putting their shit together if they want to).<br /> <br /> Point being: Humanity got better, and surely the Technocracy it's going to claim that it was all part of the plan. Which it's entirely possible, having in mind that they have the Time Sphere...but historically the Technocracy never cared about human morals when they got in the way. At least not any more than the OoR.<br /> <br /> The reason why the Technocracy get's MORE hate, howerver...I think it's because they were the underdogs figthing dragons and the evil wizards in charge back then <i>when they were playable</i>. One can't really blame them for stuff that was there before their raise to power, on an age where the Traditions were as strong if not stronger. And after that, there's no Mage: The New World to know what, say, the Craftmasons tougth about the American genoside. Probably the OoR would be the villans in that setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-11-2020, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T15:05:17-07:00","id":1387602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387259#post1387259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You're right; that's not a fair comparison. Being able to shape reality is <i>far</i> more dangerous than being able to fire a gun. The former can be abused in ways limited only by the imagination; the latter is equivalent to a single mid-level Forces rote, possibly with a touch of Correspondence for accuracy.<br /> <br /> \u2026where every demented monster and madman has infinite possibilities with which to torment others. Just look at the <b>Book of the Fallen</b>, and picture what happens when <i>everyone</i> with that mindset Awakens.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And every people with infinite possibilities to defend themselves. In a Ascended world, everyone is a godling, the fallen hide because they know they would be outmatched by everyone if they reveal their nature. Now imagine the same thing with billions of mages agaisnt the Nephandi.<br /> <br /> Plus, a gun is a tool designed for the very goal of killing. Magic is the expression of the human potential.<br /> <br /> There's only one in book reference to what could happen in a mass awakened world, in one of the scenario of Ascension, and it's not as pessimistic as you make it sound to be .<br /> <br /> &quot;The Mad Ones are expelled from the cosmos; each Quiet birth a universe that lives and dies according to it's merits. <br /> The worshipful Fallen are consigned to the Hells of their dreams: what they always truly desired. Judgment annihilates the last barriers; humanity claims the right to reward and punish itself. Technocracy triumphs in all its forms. Gray Men exult in submission to the Control of their own will; transhumanists find the key to Singularity consciousness. Every technology is immanent.<br /> Others find their Unity, their Akasha, their True Ether, their uncorrupted tongue of Enoch, all integral links in the chain of reality. That Entelechy conquers the last barriers of magic and Paradox. Joyously, they move back through Time and create themselves. Thothmes, Bh\u00e2t, the Himalayan War, MECHA, Concordia \u2014 all are part of the thread that is cast back through the ages to pull history again, to the moment of Ascension. There is always the One, but diversity \u2014 the Cycle and the Other \u2014 is never excluded. There are uncountable paradigms, but they don\u2019t chain belief or power. In the end, they are games.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T15:10:21-07:00","id":1387603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387500#post1387500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In the Bible you have people doing miracles...but it's this <b>really </b>a characteristic of the <i>common man</i>? I'm always amazed people believes religion it's *that* nice: I seem to remember that even an apostle failed to walk over water once, because he lacked enough faith. I seem to remember that faith was, indeed, able to move mountains - but for a man that had plucked his own eyes because they had dared to tempt him to sin...are these common people?<i> I find odd to think that the mage faction that's based on these stories would believe that</i> <i>everyone's faith it's equal</i>.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, the chorus is all but based on these stories. For them, the christian description of faith is only one facet of the relationship that one has with the One.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T21:32:26-07:00","id":1387646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387602#post1387602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And every people with infinite possibilities to defend themselves. In a Ascended world, everyone is a godling, the fallen hide because they know they would be outmatched by everyone if they reveal their nature. Now imagine the same thing with billions of mages agaisnt the Nephandi.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's essentially the same as a gun rights advocate's argument: if everyone has guns, then potential victims can defend themselves from predators. Your argument here assumes either that the vast majority of people are inherently good, or that Awakening makes them so; I see no reason to think that that's the case. Power corrupts, after all. Or, as M20 puts it:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The biggest problem with men and gods is that too many men consider themselves gods and too many gods share the vanities of men. This is especially true of the Awakened \u2014 men and women blessed with godlike power and cursed with human frailties.<br /> <br /> M20 p.38</div>I'll get to what <b>Ascension</b> describes shortly; but the preview is that the Nephandi aren't the only ones you need to watch out for. Indeed, if regular human beings weren't so damned <i>corruptible</i>, the Nephandi wouldn't be capable of even a fraction of the damage they can do. And they're hardly the only agents of corruption out there: the more compelling version of the Technocracy-as-antagonists that I've seen is summed up as the road to hell being paved by good intentions: the horrific practices that they engage in are largely of their own doing, motivated by the noblest of goals; but the practices they engage in are nonetheless horrific. And for the most part, the Nephandi had nothing to do with that. <br /> <br /> The Traditions are also well-intentioned. But the whole point I've been making here is that good intentions aren't enough: if you're not very careful and very wise, unintended consequences will crop up and subvert your plans for an ideal future. And the more certain you are of your rightness, the more blind you will be to those consequences. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387602#post1387602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, a gun is a tool designed for the very goal of killing. Magic is the expression of the human potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an entire Tradition that's dedicated to trying to prevent some people from expressing their human potential. They're called the Euthanatoi. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387602#post1387602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's only one in book reference to what could happen in a mass awakened world, in one of the scenario of Ascension, and it's not as pessimistic as you make it sound to be.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Mad Ones are expelled from the cosmos; each Quiet birth a universe that lives and dies according to it's merits. <br /> The worshipful Fallen are consigned to the Hells of their dreams: what they always truly desired. Judgment annihilates the last barriers; humanity claims the right to reward and punish itself. Technocracy triumphs in all its forms. Gray Men exult in submission to the Control of their own will; transhumanists find the key to Singularity consciousness. Every technology is immanent.<br /> Others find their Unity, their Akasha, their True Ether, their uncorrupted tongue of Enoch, all integral links in the chain of reality. That Entelechy conquers the last barriers of magic and Paradox. Joyously, they move back through Time and create themselves. Thothmes, Bh\u00e2t, the Himalayan War, MECHA, Concordia \u2014 all are part of the thread that is cast back through the ages to pull history again, to the moment of Ascension. There is always the One, but diversity \u2014 the Cycle and the Other \u2014 is never excluded. There are uncountable paradigms, but they don\u2019t chain belief or power. In the end, they are games.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a beautiful vision. Deeply flawed; but beautiful. And to the extent that it works, it's not merely \u201cMass Ascension\u201d; it's \u201cMass Ascension plus Deus ex Machina\u201d: that is, Telos, the Tenth Sphere of Judgment. This story element is introduced for the very first time in the scenario in question and literally nowhere else, and is almost literally a god coming down from in high and setting things right by ensuring that the wicked get punished and the just get rewarded. Without the intervention of Telos, Mass Ascension is a far less rosy prospect. <br /> <br /> Looking over the full scenario a bit more closely: <i>what causes the Marauders to be ejected into their own private Idahos?</i> What consigns the Fallen to Hells of their own making? A few paragraphs before the ones you quote, it's mentioned that most of the newly-Awakened remember their humble origins and remain humble. That's <i>not</i> typical human nature; so what's making them behave that way? The biggest single flaw of the Technocrats is that they're nosy moral busybodies who think they know how to run your life better than you do; and none of the events in the scenario up to this point are of a nature that would dissuade them from this view. So why do they suddenly switch to a live and let live philosophy? It's certainly not that they've suddenly Awakened; they've <i>been</i> Awakened this whole time, and that's been a big part of the problem. So why did not one of these things that <i>could</i> have derailed the happy ending go wrong? Arguably, Telos. <br /> <br /> \u2026though at this point, I realize that I've been getting one thing wrong: it's not Mass <i>Awakening</i> we're talking about here; it's Mass <i>Ascension</i>. Since we don't know anything about the Oracles, we really don't know what happens when someone Ascends, or even what's involved in Ascension: all that <i>is</i> known is that those who are rumored to have Ascended have never been heard from again; and the common wisdom appears to be that the path from Awakening to Ascension is a long, arduous one fraught with peril \u2014 something that must be earned through a lifetime of effort, and not something that can simply be arbitrarily bestowed upon everyone. The goal of Mass <i>Ascension</i> strikes me as the ultimate in hubris when you consider that no one knows of a reliable way to even <i>Awaken</i> someone, let alone shepherd them through to Ascension. Heck, a case could be made that the reason why the Traditions generally <i>don't</i> focus their attention on helping the Masses is because they've got their hands full with their personal efforts to achieve their <i>own</i> Ascensions. The <i>Judgment</i> scenario that you referred to isn't even a Mass Ascension scenario in the strictest sense; and the only reason why it isn't a complete and utter boondoggle is because Telos is there to guide everyone to their proper destinies. <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> And bringing it back to my original point, the Technocracy has no reason to believe that anything like Telos exists; so <i>their</i> vision of Mass Ascension isn't going to be the idealistic one described above. <i>Their</i> view of Mass Ascension is informed more by the idiotic buffoons who can't even handle the comparatively limited power that the Union has already provided them without screwing everything up. Working toward Mass Ascension under these circumstances is akin to giving the keys to the nuclear arsenal to the kids who have been beating each other over the heads with the baseball bats that you already gave them. <br /> <br /> And honestly, I doubt that most of the <i>Traditions</i> buy into the notion of Telos, either. There are several Paradigms, some quite popular, that are antithetical to there being an active principle of Judgment that hands or rewards and punishments to people as they deserve them. <i>A World of Gods and Monsters</i>, <i>Everything is Chaos</i>, <i>Everything is an Illusion, Prison, or Mistake</i>, <i>Might is Right</i>, and <i>One-Way Trip to Oblivion</i> (a favorite of the Hollow Ones) are Paradigms that don't allow for the existence of some impartial Force of Justice. So even among the <i>Traditions</i>, there's a tendency to not want to Awaken everybody; not without first preparing them to be responsible with the power that comes with Awakening. <br /> <br /> Because a Mass Awakening doesn't just unlock someone's potential to be the best they can be; it also unlocks their potential to be the <i>worst</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-13-2020, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T21:35:01-07:00","id":1387647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's an entire Tradition that's dedicated to trying to prevent some people from expressing their human potential. They're called the Euthanatoi. </div> </div> </div>That is the opposite of what the Euthanatos are about. The Euthanatos may kill you but according to their <i>justified by setting rules</i> beliefs, they believe death actually may be the best way for you to reach your potential.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T21:41:28-07:00","id":1387648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387647#post1387647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is the opposite of what the Euthanatos are about. The Euthanatos may kill you but according to their <i>justified by setting rules</i> beliefs, they believe death actually may be the best way for you to reach your potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're crossing wires here. The Euthanatos justification for their actions is that when your potential to do bad outweighs your potential to do good, murder may be warranted in order to prevent you from fulfilling your potential for evil in this life and to give you a chance to do better in your next life. That is, I'm not assuming that \u201cpotential\u201d is intrinsically good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-12-2020, 12:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T02:27:20-07:00","id":1387668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387648#post1387648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're crossing wires here. The Euthanatos justification for their actions is that when your potential to do bad outweighs your potential to do good, murder may be warranted in order to prevent you from fulfilling your potential for evil in this life and to give you a chance to do better in your next life. That is, I'm not assuming that \u201cpotential\u201d is intrinsically good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the idea was for the Euthanatos that the person to be killed is either hindering many other people's potential (killing, maiming, destroying others lives somehow) that they kinda need a reset and redirection so as not to cause an overall degredation of human potential or that they are stuck in a living hell and must be euthanized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T03:02:57-07:00","id":1387675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387500#post1387500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Chorus were to win the AW, prayer should be more effective than it's now, but not necesarilly AS effective. In the DA: Mage setting they had the dominant Paradigm over Europe, and prayers certainly *did stuff*, yet sickness and suffering were very much a thing. Would it have been different if they had the World instead? . Maybe, but I think there's enough evidence to seed plausible deniability to the idea that the Chorus can create a world where everyone can cure with a clap of their hands <i>so easily</i><br /> <br /> ...not the least because that's not how actual religion works: Not everyone it's supposed to cure with just an utterance, not a single religious belief I know suggest such a fantasyland world w/o sickness and suffering before the End of Days: Are we going to say that Christianity admiting not everyone has, nor will have, Faith before Apocalipse it's the Techncoracy's doing too?. Are we going to give Choristers such a much more hopeful worldview than any actual RL religion, as to have them sincerely believe otherwise?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh. Just to bring it up. The choristers are a lot more than just about the Christian religion and as written are about a group of people of faith trying to (and being unable to) make an ideal religion everyone can benefit from. <br /> <br /> My point is that most traditions think and believe their version of a better world is better for everone. <br /> <br /> The chorus thinks more prayers answered and more miracles guided by a benevolent &quot;One&quot; and if those who are &quot;good&quot; get more answered prayers then more people will become faithful and &quot;good&quot;, and making everyone good and full of faith would be the next step.<br /> <br /> The euthanatos thinks that if they keep people from committing atrocities on others and from undue suffering while stuck alive the overall suffering of the world will decrease creating a world where it is easier for people to develop into better people.<br /> <br /> The akashics want a world of balance and harmony where people are free to slowly or quickly gain enlightenment and greater access to the akashic wheel, developing yourself over lifetimes. <br /> <br /> The dreamspeakers think that closer toes to their gods and ancestors is great.<br /> <br /> The VR adepts think a more connected world where data is free and digital reality can improve a person's quality of life is great<br /> <br /> The etherites think adventurous science without too many restrictions will result in a better world for all.<br /> <br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> Obviously this won't work out as well as they might imagine in The world of Darkness or even a world closer to our own but...<br /> <br /> All I'm saying is that most tradition Mages are interested in making the world better for the common man. A whole bunch of them don't care, but I think the majority do in their own somewhat misguided ways.<br /> <br /> Edit: also, Christianity posits a wonderful fantasy land after the end of days. If the Christian faction of the chorus somehow won wouldn't the result be the aftermath of the end of days?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 05-12-2020, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T03:49:40-07:00","id":1387679,"title":"","content":"The Celestial Choir is a bunch of ecumenist theologians who are actually heretical to almost every religion on the planet. I've always found that amusing because everyone assumes they're a bunch of fundamentalists but they couldn't join if they were.<br /> <br /> Which is, of course, why the Knights Templar are Disparates.<br /> <br /> They AREN'T ecumenists and couldn't associate with all the other religions on an equal level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T06:17:19-07:00","id":1387695,"title":"","content":"Ever since I read Mage 2nd 20-some years ago, I've had the image of a Euthantos with a gun to someone's head, and the mage says, &quot;Maybe you'll get it right next time.&quot; Then they pull the trigger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T12:13:35-07:00","id":1387775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387679#post1387679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Celestial Choir is a bunch of ecumenist theologians who are actually heretical to almost every religion on the planet. I've always found that amusing because everyone assumes they're a bunch of fundamentalists but they couldn't join if they were.<br /> <br /> Which is, of course, why the Knights Templar are Disparates.<br /> <br /> They AREN'T ecumenists and couldn't associate with all the other religions on an equal level.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I find <i>that</i> funny because when MRev went on its kick of wiping out the Disparates and folding their remains into the Traditions, the Templar ended up in the Celestial Chorus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T12:15:13-07:00","id":1387777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387775#post1387775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I find <i>that</i> funny because when MRev went on its kick of wiping out the Disparates and folding their remains into the Traditions, the Templar ended up in the Celestial Chorus.</div> </div> </div> </div>When did that happen? I thought Revised introduced the Disparates as a group.","