-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T23:07:20-07:00","id":1387919,"title":"","content":"\u2026say the Traditions. The Crafts have their own opinions on the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T23:18:15-07:00","id":1387924,"title":"","content":"Really, the Ahl-i-Batin, of all the crafts are probably one of the most well situated. They left the Council on there own terms because of philosophical issues (namely disgust with the Council's behavior, particularly towards its own members in the 19th century) and while they were largely believed to have been driven extinct by outsiders their natural gift for secrecy allowed them to remain vital as leaders of the Web of Faith which they do to this day while also maintaining ties to Mount Qaf as the realm of correspondence and one of the foundational factions, if not the foundational faction, of the Disparate Alliance.<br /> <br /> Also their metacosmic Synergy with the universal Everything is pretty neat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T23:26:50-07:00","id":1387929,"title":"","content":"To be fair, the fluff concerning the Batini says that Mount Qaf got blown up right around the time the Batini left the Traditions \u2014 or if it wasn't blown up, the Batini lost access to it. (I think they still had access to it back during the Victorian Age; and I'm really hoping that when Victorian Age Mage comes out, one of the things it will address will be what it was like for the Batini to have Mount Qaf around.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T01:59:58-07:00","id":1387955,"title":"","content":"Suddenly want to try to run a batini + taftani game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T09:28:41-07:00","id":1388064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1387675#post1387675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh. Just to bring it up. The choristers are a lot more than just about the Christian religion and as written are about a group of people of faith trying to (and being unable to) make an ideal religion everyone can benefit from.<br /> <br /> My point is that most traditions think and believe their version of a better world is better for everone.<br /> <br /> The chorus thinks more prayers answered and more miracles guided by a benevolent &quot;One&quot; and if those who are &quot;good&quot; get more answered prayers then more people will become faithful and &quot;good&quot;, and making everyone good and full of faith would be the next step.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's all well and rigth, but that's besides my point. I'm not saying the Traditions are planning a worse world, merely pointing out a flaw of their character that &quot;could&quot; (if not checked) bring up a worse world.<br /> <br /> My point it's that prayers won't just heal w/o faith in a world where the Chorus it's dominant. We have reasons to believe Choristers reckon not all have the same amount of faith, and we know it's unrealistic to expect everyone having it. Not the least because that's not how Religion, <i>in general</i>, works. That they think (and may even be true) that everyone will get to be a &quot;holly man&quot; eventually doesn't imply that those that <i>don't </i>aren't going to have to take the short stick in such a society.<br /> <br /> They sure have reasons to expect more people will get good (as they define it) if they were in charge, but the core of the matter it's that the whole purpose of their ideal society it's for the people to get good - they don't have a plan B if this doesn't happen, because it HAS to. They don't want a world where people &quot;don't&quot; get good, and thus it's <i>feasible</i> the world would become more harsh for those that won't (depending on how much they're willing to bend for the people that don't &quot;get it&quot; vs. saying that if they don't get it it's because they're no good and deserve what happens to them).<br /> <br /> Probably if they were more dominant, there would be more &quot;holly men&quot; to help people. And if (as I believe) tech doesn't stop working, it may not be a worse world to live in (it would likely be worse for those that worship faiths that are... &quot;less represented&quot;...inside the Chorus, though. The Chorus preaches tolerace, but it's infamous for having a LOT of members that take their own religions quite seriously, and less inclined to ecumenism than maybe they should - one can only guess where these people would stand were the Chorus to win. Maybe we would have to rebel against a Theocracy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).<br /> <br /> Then again, the fact of the matter it's that &quot;making everyone good and full of faith&quot; implies that <i>those who aren't</i> are going to be left aside one way or another.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All I'm saying is that most tradition Mages are interested in making the world better for the common man. A whole bunch of them don't care, but I think the majority do in their own somewhat misguided ways. </div> </div> </div>Again, true: My post it's about HOW are they misguided.<br /> <br /> One of the reasons they're misguided it's because regardless of their good will, the &quot;man&quot; Traditions care about it's ultimately the &quot;holly man&quot;. That the Traditions believe it's feasible for everyone to be a &quot;holly man&quot;, in no way changes the fact that they don't <b>really </b>care abpout the actual <b>&quot;</b>common man&quot;. We know that even if the Technocracy it's gone not everyone will be Jesus - then you have to question what will be of the people that don't manage to be &quot;good&quot; in the meantime.<br /> <br /> If even in Horizon it's said that the life of sleepers was a hard one, one has reason to believe having the Earthly Realm under the same banner could cause sleepers similar problems, if not worse. There's a lot of hipoteticals here, but the fact it's that the Traditions ARE elitist - this comes as part and parcel with their miracles regardless of how many hugs are they willing to spare for those that haven't &quot;git gud&quot; yet (not that these aren't important), and thus if one want's to find dark here that's where you will find it.<br /> <br /> That's the difference between good, moral, Traditionalists like, say, those Extatic that follow the Code of Ananda, and those that would rather torture people into enligthenment. As it tends to be. Mage darkness comes, in most cases, from people that think their ultimately Utpical ends justify the means. This is true for every faction in the War except the Nephandi. Of course the end goal isn't going to be dark. But you can find a lot of dark places that are &quot;in between&quot; the end goal and the more prosaic realities of the WoD.<br /> <br /> In the case of the Traditions, it's that the common man has no real place in their ultimate utopy - their best case scenario to end all best case scenarios it's, as you describe, that everyone will have some magick and thus there will be <i>no muggle </i><i>left</i>.<br /> <br /> This is a character flaw that manifests serveral ways (and differently in different Traditions): From the unethical wizards that find shelter within the Traditions (that aren't the majority of Traditionalists, but neither a negligible number. I can name whole factions of them) to defending morals that may put lives of humans aside to favor spirits or bygones. Perhaps even refusing to mass produce miracles. Traditionalists don't have to have this flaw, and a victory of the Traditions could potentially avoid it, but it's still a very common, very defining, flaw. Common enough to be part of basically every Tradition book, and a good place to make the Traditions not be unequivocally, inherently, good.<br /> <br /> To be perfectly clear: If people persist in saying that the Traditions are good because they expect every person to have magick and wonder...Then I can equally deny all the evil of the Techncoracy because they too want a perfect world where everyone has science and creativity. The diference in their ends are semantic (Ascencion vs Empowerment), the differences in their methods, however, aren't semantic...and both reveal a ton of darkness here (and no small amount of virtue, mind you, but this thread it's about the flaws not the merits).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: also, Christianity posits a wonderful fantasy land after the end of days. If the Christian faction of the chorus somehow won wouldn't the result be the aftermath of the end of days? </div> </div> </div>That would be more like Mass Ascencion. Many mages think winning the War it's the main step before reaching it, that would be the best case scenario to end all best case scenarios (others think the War it's an effort born of <i>tirany</i>, and thus will never bring true utopy). In any case: No, I don't think winning would be enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-13-2020, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T12:12:15-07:00","id":1388109,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> Mainly I was just clarifying my position as it seemed my statements weren't fully understood or thought to mean I think the Traditions are doing good. Rather than I simply mean that most of their members mean well for even the common man. <br /> <br /> That they don't care for the &quot;common man&quot; is also part of where I disagree. I would argue that the Akashics and ecstatics simply think that the common man is simply at an earlier stage of learning and mostly care for preserving a world where they can follow the path to enlightenment/nirvannah. That the &quot;common man&quot; of the dreamspeakers are the people of those cultures displaced mostly by western ones who want to be free to worship and commune with the spirits without being told they are foolish barbarians, and want to preserve them from the fate of the common man of the verbena whose cultures, more or less no longer exist, that the choristers do care about the common man and the people who can't be holy men will be shepherded and defended by the holy man until such a time that they can be holy men, that at least some of the etherites want to bring science to the common man and one of them tried to unite the world after all, that the VA are representative of the future common man. So they kinda care but are generally ineffectual at helping the common man on a large scale. <br /> <br /> And to your other point. I do equally deny the evil of both the Traditions and the Technocracy. To classify either as good or bad would be a gross oversimplification of two organizations. That would be a bit like saying a country is good or bad. I find saying the Traditions don't care about the common man is similarly absurd. <br /> <br /> As for what last bit, the end result of them winning would then be the period before the end of days, no real opposition to their consensus, and the eventual arrival and that fantasy land afterwards then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T12:16:35-07:00","id":1388111,"title":"","content":"A large part of whether the Traditions work or not seems to be [from this thread and other places] whether you think that if the Union ever fell or even a permanent peace treaty happened whether or not you'd think the other Traditions would try to create:<br /> <br /> 1. A reality where their paradigm rules<br /> 2. A reality where everyone can choose their own path to enlightenment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T13:50:47-07:00","id":1388147,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12480_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12480\" data-vbnamecard=\"12480\">Spacecat</a>: while we're clarifying positions, let me clarify that the perspectives that I've been offering in this thread have been intentionally biased against the Traditions. Not because I don't like them; I do. But because the point of this thread <i>is</i> to show how you can present the Traditions as antagonists without actually changing them \u2014 just by putting your attention on their flaws. In particular, I'm trying to point out unintended consequences of the Traditions' views \u2014 not merely \u201cthey have virtues and flaws\u201d, but \u201chere are ways that even their virtues can lead to bad outcomes\u201d. <br /> <br /> In a more balanced view, I do agree that the Traditions typically <i>do</i> care about the Sleepers. But as a group, they do so from the perspective of \u201cthe best thing for Sleepers is to Awaken\u201d; and they tend to care for Sleepers by trying to find ways to Awaken them. They don't even bother trying to find ways to ask Sleepers if they <i>want</i> to be Awakened; they assume that it's such a positive good that nobody would refuse it, or they assume that Sleepers aren't equipped to answer the question until after they've Awakened. Or both. <br /> <br /> <i>And</i> they tend not to ask whether or not there are some Sleepers who <i>shouldn't</i> Awaken, which is what my most recent posts have focused on: that there are people who are too crazy, evil, or merely irresponsible for Awakening them to be a good thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-13-2020, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T15:28:55-07:00","id":1388167,"title":"","content":"I remember the Book of Chantries was what introduced me to the &quot;bad&quot; Traditions with the House of Helekar (that the Traditions are ignorant enough to let run) and Doissetep where everyone was at each other's throats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T17:03:47-07:00","id":1388188,"title":"","content":"Both Helekar, and Doissetep, played major roles in the failure of the Tradition Council, and Doissetep's civil war and destruction helped make the Avatar Storm worse. No Technocracy Construct so actively made things worse in the same way the Tradition chantries did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T17:19:04-07:00","id":1388191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1388188#post1388188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both Helekar, and Doissetep, played major roles in the failure of the Tradition Council, and Doisse