n-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T00:13:10-07:00","id":1388254,"title":"","content":"Three quarters of the Void Engineers, from what I hear tell. <br /> <br /> Though what if it wasn't nearly as many as were reported? What if a contingent of the VEs were <i>prepared</i> for what happened, and took the opportunity to jump ship and disappear into the depths of the Void, and are incorrectly presumed dead? If even a third of the losses turn out instead to be part of this faction, you could have two versions of the Void Engineers, one not unlike its pre-Anomaly version (i.e., not particularly militant, and far more interested in exploration than defense) but gone rogue, and the other essentially being the militant post-Anomaly version of the Convention, defending Earth from Threat Null.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T21:05:03-07:00","id":1388552,"title":"","content":"Mages are filled with hubris and privileged towards wraiths, yes. Even when they try not to:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Book of Oblivion, p. 48</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b>The Arcane Storm</b></i><br /> <br /> One of the most dangerous storms that appears with some regularity is the Arcane Storm. When a mage dies and becomes a wraith, their avatar rips away, inverts, and creates a small tornado, which causes magical changes to the Tempest.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Visual Cues: A tornado crackling with energy drops down and tears up the Tempest in its wake.<br /> \u2022 Sensory Experience: The scent of ozone can be smelled wherever the tornado is seen.<br /> \u2022 Damage: A wraith caught in the tornado takes damage from the magick whirling in its wake. The Storyteller is encouraged to combine elemental effects, such as fire and earth or acid and ice, or to hasten the flow of time or drain Corpus from a victim of this attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T14:44:45-07:00","id":1392319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386239#post1386239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, which doesn't mean it's not true.<br /> <br /> Mind you, a lot of people took the Revised Covention Books as objectively true. The Iteration X book being the worst.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that their 1e book portrayed them as really uber evil (i.e. a mash-up of Skynet, the Galactic Empire, and the Borg) I can understand why their Revised write-up swerved far away from that ... but too much IMO, to the point you'd think they were the noblest faction in the setting. They essentially jumped straight from being bland villains to bland heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1410,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","user":"Czernobog","date":". 05-28-2020, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T15:52:36-07:00","id":1392342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1388240#post1388240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was one guy who triggered it. Arguably, it could only be triggered because the conditions were ripe for it to be triggered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it wasn't Jones's fault. The nuke used by the Smiling Lord against the ghost of Enoch in the Underworld that the True Black Hand was using as their headquarters during the battle between Stygia and the TBH (which itself was setup by Anubis and the Ferrymen) was used first. The shockwaves from that first nuke triggered Jones's nuke before he had even reached where he was going to use it for his experiment.<br /> <br /> Yeah, Jones bares some blame for it but the Smiling Lord, the Ferrymen and Anubis all hold more blame for it than him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T16:55:44-07:00","id":1396532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1386704#post1386704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As <i>Enginseer-42 </i>said, it's true that in M20 (and sometimes elsewhere) it's suggested that tech works bad (or not at all) if the Paradigm doesn't support it, however it's also implied that mundane tech only trully stops working in the most remote areas of the Earth. Or in specific Umbral landscapes. Places like that can reasonably be said to be outside of what Traditional <b>ideal </b>&quot;terraforming&quot; does.<br /> <br /> Much more representative of the state of science and technology in a victory of the Traditions it's what they did in Horizon. Mages rule, people have phones and flying carpets...but they also have man-eating dragons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I quite literally have the book on Horizon, and it plainly states that while they managed to create a shared space where their respective mystic paradigms were coincidental, technological magic such as the SoEs' and VAs' stuff remained vulgar outside their specific areas (and mystical paradigms were vulgar inside those spaces).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T18:27:33-07:00","id":1396772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions?p=1392319#post1392319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering that their 1e book portrayed them as really uber evil (i.e. a mash-up of Skynet, the Galactic Empire, and the Borg) I can understand why their Revised write-up swerved far away from that ... but too much IMO, to the point you'd think they were the noblest faction in the setting. They essentially jumped straight from being bland villains to bland heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly preferred to play them as a mashup of both. The revised take certainly isn't wrong, it's just a very optimistic take. Underneath it all is a convention that's prided itself on turning themselves into a weapon. An apolitical war machine with no goals beyond excelling at what they do.... Suddenly forced to ask those questions because command is gone.<br /> <br /> Which has lead them to the knight errant, cyborg paladin behavior you see in the revised book. They're soldiers in search of a war to fight. And the transition certainly isn't stable or without conflict. Some iterators want to keep fighting traditionalists. Some want to go vigilante on hemophages, some want to wipe out pixies.<br /> <br /> But they are, at their hearts, a hammer in search of a nail. With the question being still up in the air as to whether they'll ultimately break from their brutal past, or if the inertia is too much to turn aside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}